                                                "value": "Choose the discrete incompressible liquid momentum/pressure formulation, viscosity treatment, face fluxes, and conservative advection/diffusion for the declared species. Specify compatible open/pressure outer conditions, pressure null-space treatment where applicable, and initial/boundary data. Keep geometry operators abstract only at the explicit interface consumed by T-geometry-design. Define separate stationary-flow and species-transport implementation boundaries: flow exposes committed/staged conservative fluxes, accessible volumes and boundary accounts without requiring the species solver. Species transport later consumes these interfaces with moving geometry and the qualified passive schedule. Specify any bounded early tracer/reference probe separately from production species transport; it must not establish species positivity, diffusion, or full transport acceptance."
                                            }
