                                {
                                    "edit": {
                                        "op": "add_task",
                                        "task": {
                                            "acceptance_criteria": [
                                                "The approved passive references and repeated-cycle/refinement comparisons are executed or explicitly reported unverified, with local and cumulative errors compared against the frozen budgets.",
                                                "Hard monitors and selected complete committed-state inspections cover declared relaxation, forcing and accumulation timescales; horizons, extension/stopping rationale and unresolved drift are recorded.",
                                                "Injected failures and retry exhaustion report preservation of all authoritative passive owners and committed time, with requested versus actual simulated intervals.",
                                                "Complete interval cost and memory include staging, geometry, mechanics, contents, pressure/coupling iterations, safety work, rejected attempts and commit; hardware, build, precision and workers are recorded under A-hardware.",
                                                "The report retains decisive configurations and counterexamples, distinguishes pass/reject/inconclusive findings from experiment completion, and states that species, active behavior and population suitability remain unqualified."
                                            ],
                                            "components": [
                                                "C-evidence",
                                                "C-state",
                                                "C-structure",
                                                "C-contents",
                                                "C-field",
                                                "C-interface"
                                            ],
                                            "context": "Consume AR-passive-coupling and the human-approved AR-work-package. Run its bounded passive campaign with closed ports and no metabolism, controller, actuator, or full species solver. Cover equilibrium, translation/rotation, free expansion, compression/recovery, moving barriers/corners, supported narrow passages and support changes as specified. Use externally applied loads with explicit work accounts for repeated compression cycles and separate closed unforced cases. Compare approved resolutions/timesteps at equal simulated durations; assess local geometry/volume, pressure, shape, reactions, wall work, weak-motion loss, passive propulsion, cyclic gain and accumulated drift. Inject coupling failures and exercise bounded retry exhaustion. Use simulation-health and traces capabilities with implemented project oracles and telemetry, controlled configurations, meaningful scales and justified horizons; record actual commands, source/build/hardware identity, observations, tolerances and limits in supported MindGraph result fields. Preserve compact findings under .codex/runs. Do not weaken approved limits or claim active/population adoption. A negative or inconclusive completed campaign blocks downstream reliance pending review.",
                                            "depends_on": [
