                        "id": "review-155318c083501f50b20235b1e1fb68e6",
                        "question": "Review the current T-pilot worker result against its own acceptance criteria. The previous review concluded that the pilot succeeded at diagnostic wiring and should proceed to T-loop, but its issues status still blocks that prerequisite. Inspect the decisive retained evidence, including the WebP snapshot through project_inspect image, and the task requirements. Determine whether there is actual incomplete required work or only reported limitations outside the pilot scope (including later standalone-package qualification). If the supplied current evidence satisfies the task, record explicit accepted_results with a reason for the limitations; otherwise propose the smallest real repair. Do not manufacture evidence, rerun the pilot, accept physics or human approval, or edit the accepted plan merely to work around a management defect. The worker deliberately reported inconclusive physics because the task requested that review-handling exercise; no physical algorithm was tested.",
