            "response": "{\n  \"architecture\": {\n    \"components\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-core\",\n        \"name\": \"Authoritative simulation state and advancement\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own physical state, stable structural identities, units, elapsed simulated time, bounded advancement, validity checks, and atomic commit. Expose construction, observation, and advance interfaces independent of Bitloop scenes.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-structures\",\n        \"name\": \"Structures and chamber contents\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own connected deformable elements, contractile fibers, structural contact, membrane geometry, and well-mixed chamber inventories. Relate chamber pressure, contents inertia, occupied area, and wall work consistently.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-fields\",\n        \"name\": \"Resolved fluid and transported amounts\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own grid fluid state and species amounts. Compute conservative face transport, pressure response, and moving-boundary interaction without mixing across intact membranes.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-exchanges\",\n        \"name\": \"Coupling and physical exchanges\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Coordinate geometric displacement, paired impulses, pressure work, and finite inventory transfers between authoritative owners. Keep numerical residuals separate from physical energy and metabolic resources.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-experiments\",\n        \"name\": \"Construction, control, and reference fixtures\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Construct representative organisms and physical references, implement constrained local sensing and fuel-limited actuation, and define deterministic workloads outside the physics core.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-shell\",\n        \"name\": \"Bitloop shell and evidence adapters\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Keep generated Substrate files thin; adapt configuration, fixed-time advancement, drawing, semantic traces, snapshots, and explicit restart state to existing Bitloop facilities.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"decisions\": [\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Limit this initial plan to a supervised tooling pilot, an approved numerical experiment contract, a coupled organism proof, and a 16-organism laboratory qualification. Do not implement the rich world or scaling ambition yet.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-scope\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The vision explicitly requires proof of the inexpensive coupled foundation before broad feature accumulation. The later workloads remain requirements for subsequent planning, not claims delivered here.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Provisionally use connected compliant area-bearing elements and fibers, well-mixed pressure chambers, and a conservative staggered-grid fluid with explicit membrane-side control volumes. Investigate bounded small-cell aggregation only within connected fluid on the same side of a barrier.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-numerics\",\n        \"rationale\": \"This directly tests the preferred specialized-representation hypothesis. Exact discretization, coupling order, stabilization, and support limits must be frozen by T-contract and approved before implementation; method suitability remains experimentally unresolved.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Use one authoritative owner for each amount and one advancement schedule. Define explicit paired transfers of amounts, impulses, and work, and stage changed state until the requested interval is valid.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-state\",\n        \"rationale\": \"This prevents inventory duplication, inconsistent pressure geometry, and skipped failed intervals without requiring a full-world copy for each tiny substep.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Publish a small fixed resolution range, bounded solver work, and explicit unsupported-condition errors. Do not add automatic representation switching, adaptive remeshing, GPU execution, or a selectable solver framework.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-bounds\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Bounded scope makes cost and physical validity falsifiable before investing in generality.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Use project-owned adapters to existing Bitloop diagnostics; keep tests and observational output outside the physical core. No framework or sibling changes are authorized by this plan.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-boundary\",\n        \"rationale\": \"This preserves independent project ownership and avoids duplicating available infrastructure.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Freeze tolerances and performance interpretation before candidate comparisons. Adoption requires both local physical behavior and complete-interval cost; negative or inconclusive experiment results are valid deliverables, not permission to proceed.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-gates\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The predecessor failures demonstrate that global balances, attractive rendering, and fast isolated kernels cannot establish suitability.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relationships\": [\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-core\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Owns and advances authoritative states implemented by\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structures\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-core\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Owns and advances authoritative states implemented by\",\n        \"to\": \"C-fields\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-core\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Schedules paired exchanges and validates their commit through\",\n        \"to\": \"C-exchanges\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-exchanges\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Consumes membrane geometry and pairs wall reactions and chamber transfers with\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structures\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-exchanges\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Pairs boundary displacement, fluid reactions, and species transfers with\",\n        \"to\": \"C-fields\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-experiments\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Constructs state and submits constrained local control requests to\",\n        \"to\": \"C-core\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-shell\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Hosts selected fixtures and presents their diagnostics through\",\n        \"to\": \"C-experiments\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-shell\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Calls advancement and reads committed state without owning physics through\",\n        \"to\": \"C-core\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"summary\": \"Build a bounded CPU proof of explicit compliant organisms coupled to conservative spatial fluid and transport fields, using inexpensive chambers only where well-mixed contents are physically appropriate. First establish the tooling loop and freeze an approved numerical contract. Then implement and qualify the mechanics and moving-boundary field foundations, integrate a resource-limited organism, and measure a shared 16-organism laboratory. Stop for evidence-backed reconsideration if physical or complete-cost gates fail; broader biology and the 256-organism rich world follow only through a later approved plan.\"\n  },\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Minimal runnable Substrate diagnostic fixture, actual build and scene configuration, and retained findings from the supervised execution, saved-result, review, and reload loop.\",\n      \"id\": \"A-pilot\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-pilot\",\n      \"title\": \"Supervised Bitloop pilot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Versioned physical and numerical experiment specification: interfaces, authoritative ownership, units, supported scales, equations and advancement order, fixed acceptance budgets, bounded experiments, workloads, and explicit exclusions.\",\n      \"id\": \"A-contract\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-contract\",\n      \"title\": \"Coupled proof contract\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Project-owned advancement interface, committed-state representation, stable references, staged updates, failure semantics, and focused transaction tests.\",\n      \"id\": \"A-core\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-core\",\n      \"title\": \"Transactional core foundation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Compliant structures and chamber implementation with independent physical references, inertia and pressure-work findings, supported range, and measured kernel-plus-staging costs.\",\n      \"id\": \"A-structures\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-structures\",\n      \"title\": \"Structure and chamber candidate\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Conservative moving-boundary field implementation and bounded experiment findings for local volume, barrier integrity, geometry transitions, pressure convergence, transport, and full field cost.\",\n      \"id\": \"A-fields\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-fields\",\n      \"title\": \"Moving-boundary field candidate\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Runnable coupled physical fixture and decision-bearing report covering deformation, chamber loading, two-way fluid coupling, nutrient exchange, prescribed actuation, and complete-step cost.\",\n      \"id\": \"A-coupled\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-coupled\",\n      \"title\": \"Coupled physical proof\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"A locally sensing, metabolizing organism and two-chamber pumping fixture using the same physical interfaces, with explicit fuel and reaction accounting and reproducible demonstrations.\",\n      \"id\": \"A-active\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-active\",\n      \"title\": \"Resource-limited organism demonstration\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Explicit restart serialization and configuration compatibility rules, with uninterrupted-versus-restored continuation evidence and deterministic replay limits.\",\n      \"id\": \"A-restart\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-restart\",\n      \"title\": \"Validated experiment restart\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Reproducible 16-organism shared laboratory, inspected recordings, complete-cost measurements, long-horizon physical findings, published validity limits, and recommendation about readiness for a separately planned rich world.\",\n      \"id\": \"A-laboratory\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-laboratory\",\n      \"title\": \"Laboratory qualification package\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AS-scope\",\n      \"statement\": \"The requested first plan should authorize only the bounded foundation campaign described in D-scope, rather than the entire long-term vision.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AS-hardware\",\n      \"statement\": \"Access to the proposed Ryzen 9 9950X3D reference machine is not established. Other hardware may support development and rejection screens, but cannot establish the reference-machine performance claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AS-environment\",\n      \"statement\": \"The first habitat is liquid-filled and has no resolved free surface. Well-mixed chambers are restricted to fixtures whose behavior does not require internal sloshing, circulation, or stratification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AS-approval\",\n      \"statement\": \"The numerical implementation and laboratory workload budgets are provisional until the explicit human checkpoint in T-approval. Applying this plan alone does not approve those choices.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Identify the actual target, project-owned build context, development flags, stable scene ID, and available diagnostic hooks; compile the smallest relevant target.\",\n        \"Run a deterministic, nonphysical fixture with an implemented semantic metric and inspect an actual snapshot. Retain actual commands, configuration, observations, and compact evidence.\",\n        \"Under human supervision, demonstrate execution, supported mindgraph-result observations, saved result, review, and reload without inventing management APIs or changing their owning project.\",\n        \"Record instruction conflicts, missing hooks, evidence loss, and unavailable management operations explicitly; a partial loop is not reported as a successful pilot.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-shell\"],\n      \"context\": \"Use capabilities bitloop, traces, and snapshots-checkpoints: .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/snapshots-checkpoints.md; start with .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md and relevant tracing-diagnostics.md and checkpoints-snapshots.md references. Inspect worker-local instructions and active headers. Generated trace and checkpoint hooks are not presumed implemented. Follow D-boundary; exclude physics implementation and framework repairs. All subsequent tasks retain tested claims, source/build identity, actual commands, failed/skipped checks, compact conclusions, and relevant evidence under .codex/runs; decision-bearing findings belong in supported summary, checks[].name, issues, and plan_concern fields.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"goal\": \"Establish the smallest supervised workflow that can carry trustworthy implementation evidence.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-pilot\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does the observed execution/save/review/reload loop preserve enough substantive evidence and ownership context to safely schedule the numerical campaign, or must management problems be resolved in their owning project first?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Run the supervised tooling pilot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Specify 2D units, conserved inventories, chamber mass and inertia treatment, material versus numerical state, stable references, transfer records, advance results, and unsupported-condition errors.\",\n        \"Choose exact candidate mechanics, pressure and transport discretizations, membrane geometry representation, same-side small-cell treatment, coupling order, iteration/substep limits, and staged-commit strategy.\",\n        \"Predeclare local and cumulative error budgets relative to useful motion and resource flow, physical reference oracles, resolution comparisons, horizons, and rejection conditions; do not use total background energy to normalize meaningful errors.\",\n        \"Freeze coupled-proof and 16-organism laboratory geometry, coefficients, activity, minimum feature sizes, two chambers and 16 actuators per organism, up to 128 vertices each, and 128 by 128 active environmental cells.\",\n        \"Specify the laboratory real-time target, complete timing boundaries, memory accounting, hardware requirements, recording measurements, and bounded experimental effort. Keep rich-world targets documented as later requirements.\",\n        \"Provide concrete runnable fixture requirements and identify any requirement tradeoffs for human approval before implementation.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-core\", \"C-structures\", \"C-fields\", \"C-exchanges\", \"C-experiments\"],\n      \"context\": \"Consume A-pilot for the actual diagnostic/build constraints. Resolve the shared interfaces and numerical choices left provisional in D-numerics, D-state, and D-gates; this task specifies rather than implements the solver. Include uniform-pressure equilibrium, free expansion, translation/rotation, compression/recovery, advection/diffusion, sealed moving barriers, changing geometric support, narrow supported passages, and passive energy tests. Define finite opening/permeability transport and reject chamber models that conceal unsupported inertia or local flow behavior. Capability simulation-health, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md, supplies the diagnostic workflow, not the physical oracle.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-pilot\"],\n      \"goal\": \"Turn the provisional representation into a falsifiable, bounded, implementation-ready experiment.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-contract\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"A-pilot\"],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Define the numerical and acceptance contract\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Present A-contract and its unresolved tradeoffs to the human, explicitly including approximation budgets, chamber inertia, membrane support limits, workload scope, and performance interpretation.\",\n        \"Record an explicit approval of the identified contract version before dependent implementation is released.\",\n        \"If approval is withheld or material changes are requested, keep the gate closed and request a plan/contract revision; report existence alone is not approval.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-core\", \"C-structures\", \"C-fields\", \"C-exchanges\"],\n      \"context\": \"This is the human decision point required by AS-approval and the vision's approved first physical work package. Do not reinterpret silence, plan application, or automated review as numerical approval. No implementation or framework authorization is included in this task.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-contract\"],\n      \"goal\": \"Obtain explicit permission to execute the bounded numerical campaign.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-approval\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"A-contract\"],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Approve the coupled experiment scope\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement the approved construction, observation, exchange-record, and advancement interfaces without scene, rendering, trace-format, or file-output dependencies in the core.\",\n        \"Verify requested intervals advance exactly to their committed simulated time, independent of rendering cadence.\",\n        \"Inject invalid state, exhausted work limits, and failed attempts; verify authoritative state and time remain at the last valid commit with explicit failure details.\",\n        \"Test stable references and single inventory ownership, and measure staging overhead on representative field and structural state sizes without unnecessary per-substep full copies.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-core\"],\n      \"context\": \"Implement A-contract under D-state and D-boundary after T-approval. This package owns advancement and transaction infrastructure only, not physical kernels. Use capability bitloop, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md, for the existing CMake and math integration; compile the smallest relevant target and retain focused test observations.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-contract\", \"T-approval\"],\n      \"goal\": \"Provide the small authoritative core used by both physical representations.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-core\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"A-contract\"],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement authoritative state and bounded advancement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement approved compliant elements, prescribed fiber actuation, membrane geometry, contact, and chamber pressure/inventory mechanics through A-core.\",\n        \"Measure translation/rotation, compression/recovery, uniform chamber pressure, deformation error, and passive cyclic energy behavior against A-contract.\",\n        \"Demonstrate chamber contents contribute declared mass and inertia, pressure work uses actual chamber geometry, and transfers do not duplicate inventory.\",\n        \"Report feature degeneracy, timestep sensitivity, work limits, staging cost, and failed or inconclusive gates; preserve minimal counterexamples.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-core\", \"C-structures\"],\n      \"context\": \"Consume A-contract and A-core. Use a mechanical harness with prescribed external loads; do not implement resolved fluid, controllers, growth, or general fracture. Use simulation-health and traces via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, and the simulation-health-diagnostics.md and tracing-diagnostics.md skill references. Implement required semantic metrics and distinguish numerical residual from fuel or heat.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-contract\", \"T-core\"],\n      \"goal\": \"Test whether inexpensive structures and chambers satisfy their independent physical obligations.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-structures\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"A-contract\", \"A-core\"],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Do the measured deformation, contents inertia, pressure-work, and passive-cycle results support the approved cheap chamber and compliant mechanics model, or does D-numerics require revision before coupling?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Implement and test structures and pressure chambers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement approved fluid pressure and conservative transport with prescribed moving membranes using the shared geometry interface.\",\n        \"Measure local volume and pressure fields for rest, free expansion, advection, diffusion, and moving sealed boundaries; check local references independently of global balances.\",\n        \"Exercise moving corners, changing cut-cell support, and minimum-width supported passages. Verify no cross-membrane interpolation or forbidden species flux.\",\n        \"Report convergence, timestep restrictions, small-cell handling, memory, geometry rebuilds, pressure-solve work, and complete field-interval cost across the frozen resolutions.\",\n        \"Retain negative and inconclusive findings without relaxing budgets or adding unapproved corrections.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-core\", \"C-fields\", \"C-exchanges\"],\n      \"context\": \"Consume A-contract and A-core; use prescribed boundary motion rather than waiting for the structural solver. This is the bounded feasibility experiment for D-numerics, not a stationary bulk benchmark. Use simulation-health and traces with .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md and their routed skill references. Unsupported geometry must fail explicitly, not erase walls or merge incompatible fluid.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-contract\", \"T-core\"],\n      \"goal\": \"Expose the moving-boundary field's physical and computational risks before organism integration.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-fields\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"A-contract\", \"A-core\"],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Do local geometry/transport consistency, barrier integrity, support-transition behavior, and complete moving-boundary cost justify retaining D-numerics, or is a different representation required before coupled work?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Test conservative flow with moving thin barriers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Integrate deformable tissue, a pressure chamber, external fluid, finite nutrient exchange, and prescribed actuation with paired impulses and pressure work.\",\n        \"Show useful motion and measured transport in the approved fixture; compare passive controls and refinement so numerical propulsion or erased weak motion cannot explain success.\",\n        \"Check local displacement, inventory, momentum/work accounts, pressure equilibrium, barrier integrity, and committed-state validity over the approved coupled horizons.\",\n        \"Measure complete calculated intervals including preparation, neighborhood work, coupling iterations, safety checks, retries, and commit; expose pressure and staging costs separately.\",\n        \"Provide a runnable headless demonstration, semantic findings, and inspected snapshots. Preserve failure examples and explicitly distinguish experiment completion from adoption.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-core\", \"C-structures\", \"C-fields\", \"C-exchanges\", \"C-experiments\", \"C-shell\"],\n      \"context\": \"Proceed only if reviews of A-structures and A-fields release their foundation. Consume their actual supported ranges plus A-contract and A-core. Implement physical coupling, not metabolic controllers yet. Use bitloop, traces, simulation-health, and snapshots-checkpoints via their .mindgraph/project_capabilities/*.md hints and the relevant development skill references, including visual-qa.md. Visual evidence must be correlated with authoritative state.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-contract\", \"T-core\", \"T-structures\", \"T-fields\"],\n      \"goal\": \"Determine whether individually plausible representations remain coherent and affordable when coupled.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-coupled\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"A-contract\", \"A-core\", \"A-structures\", \"A-fields\"],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does the complete coupled trajectory preserve the approved local behavior and error budgets at representative cost, or should the foundation be rejected before adding resource-limited biology and population workloads?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Demonstrate the coupled physical proof\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement constrained local sensing, deterministic control, explicit reaction inputs/outputs, nutrient uptake, fuel-limited contraction, and waste production outside the numerical kernels.\",\n        \"Show that exhausted fuel limits activity and that numerical loss or residual accounts cannot replenish fuel.\",\n        \"Demonstrate a moving organism and a two-chamber pump built from the same primitives; measure finite transport and useful pump work against passive and blocked-channel controls.\",\n        \"Verify resource balances and meaningful behavior under the approved resolution comparison, with no organism-type physics in the core.\",\n        \"Provide runnable configurations and inspected trace/snapshot evidence for the active demonstrations.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-experiments\", \"C-exchanges\", \"C-shell\"],\n      \"context\": \"Consume A-coupled and A-contract after the coupled review releases work. Keep construction and controller interfaces within the approved local-information and resource constraints. Exclude heredity, general brains, growth, damage/repair, and broad chemistry from this initial proof. Use traces, simulation-health, and snapshots-checkpoints through their catalogue hint files and relevant skill references; retain actual rates, resource flows, periods, simulated horizons, and limits.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-contract\", \"T-coupled\"],\n      \"goal\": \"Turn the physical proof into genuinely active, resource-constrained organism behavior.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-active\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"A-contract\", \"A-coupled\"],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Add local control and resource-limited activity\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Serialize authoritative physical state, controller state, configuration identity, simulated time, and random state required for continuation; exclude reconstructible caches.\",\n        \"Reject incompatible checkpoint/configuration combinations without changing the last valid state.\",\n        \"Compare uninterrupted and restored continuation through active pumping and contact using fingerprints or the approved tolerances, inventory checks, and behavioral observables.\",\n        \"Document deterministic replay limits and measured checkpoint/recording overhead using actual Bitloop hooks rather than assuming generated hooks work.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-core\", \"C-experiments\", \"C-shell\"],\n      \"context\": \"Consume A-active and A-contract. Use snapshots-checkpoints and traces: .mindgraph/project_capabilities/snapshots-checkpoints.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, and checkpoints-snapshots.md and tracing-diagnostics.md references. This implements explicit restart for the demonstrated state only, not a general serialization framework.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-contract\", \"T-active\"],\n      \"goal\": \"Make the active experiment reproducibly restartable before relying on long recorded runs.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-restart\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"A-contract\", \"A-active\"],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement and validate active-state restart\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Run the frozen 16-organism shared habitat with all organisms sensing, consuming fuel, and actuating, including shared flow, contact, pumping, feeding, and declared exchange.\",\n        \"Measure at least one simulated second per wall-clock second on the approved reference configuration, or explicitly report failure/unverified reference performance. Include all substeps, retries, checks, and commit costs.\",\n        \"Report active vertices, elements/bonds, actuators, field work, controller work, event rates, worker configuration, hardware/compiler/precision, competing load, memory, mean/tail/maximum latency, and separate rendering, recording, and checkpoint costs.\",\n        \"Run the predeclared behavioral horizon with continuous hard-condition monitors, selected complete-state inspections, repeated activity/contact windows, and refinement comparisons; extend while drift remains unresolved within the approved experiment bound.\",\n        \"Provide an inspectable recording and concrete replay command. Report local physical findings, accumulated residuals, worst cases, stopping rationale, unsupported conditions, and remaining uncertainty.\",\n        \"Conclude only laboratory readiness or rejection. Do not infer acceptance of the 256-organism, ten-simulated-minute rich-world workload from this result.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\"C-core\", \"C-structures\", \"C-fields\", \"C-exchanges\", \"C-experiments\", \"C-shell\"],\n      \"context\": \"Consume A-contract, A-active, and A-restart. Qualify D-scope rather than silently expanding to thermal state, damage/repair, or scaling ambitions. Use existing bitloop, traces, simulation-health, and snapshots-checkpoints workflows via their catalogue hint files and skill references. Retain compact decision-bearing results and reproducible configurations; high-volume temporary probes remain development-only and are cleaned after findings are retained. A failed quality gate cannot be traded away to meet speed.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-contract\", \"T-active\", \"T-restart\"],\n      \"goal\": \"Establish whether the first shared active laboratory is physically useful, reproducible, and affordable.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-laboratory\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"A-contract\", \"A-active\", \"A-restart\"],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Do the laboratory's complete-cost, interaction, restart, and accumulated-error results justify planning the 256-organism rich world, or must representation, supported quality, or an explicitly human-approved requirement tradeoff be revisited first?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Qualify the shared active laboratory\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"vision_summary\": \"Substrate aims to support rich, long-running biological experiments through physically coherent interactions among deformable structures, fluid, transported resources, and locally constrained controllers. This initial plan proves the uncertain coupled foundation and a small active shared laboratory before committing to hundreds of organisms, damage and repair, thermal processes, or evolution.\"\n}",
