rmeability transfers and local reaction stoichiometry/rates with unique inventory ownership.\",\n        \"Worked advection, diffusion, two-chamber equilibration and membrane transport examples specify local concentration accuracy, positivity and conservation oracles.\",\n        \"Specify chemical energy consumption, actuator work limits and numerical-loss exclusion; define gradient-preservation thresholds before comparison.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-biology\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Use accepted passive interfaces. Choose a small declared nutrient/fuel/waste/signal set with explicit mass/energy meaning, positivity treatment and finite channel/permeability laws. Thermal transport and rupture/repair implementation remain later scope.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-passive\",\n        \"T-contract\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Define the downstream conservative transport and resource laws after passive feasibility.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-design-transport\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"F-passive\",\n        \"F-contract\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Design finite species transport and metabolic exchanges\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"F-transport supplies field/chamber species ownership and finite-rate transfer APIs with focused tests.\",\n        \"Advection/diffusion references quantify local error and numerical diffusion; connected chambers do not mix instantaneously.\",\n        \"Moving intact impermeable membranes block species; permeable interfaces have measured paired flux and no negative inventories.\",\n        \"Transport failure rolls back the whole attempted interval, including geometry and mechanics.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-boundary\"\n      ],\n      \"con