                            "summary": "One project-owned simulation core maintains authoritative committed state and a bounded transactional advancement schedule. Compact structural mechanics, chamber contents, and fluid control volumes have disjoint ownership of mass and species. A shared geometry/exchange layer makes occupied area, boundary flux, pressure work, and collision barriers agree. Local controllers submit resource-limited requests rather than modifying physical state. A thin Bitloop shell provides construction, presentation, replay, and project-owned diagnostic adapters. Numerical adoption is conditional, not implied by construction."
