                                        "edit": {
                                            "op": "add_task",
                                            "task": {
                                                "acceptance_criteria": [
                                                    "Uniform advection and diffusion satisfy approved local concentration/profile, global amount and refinement references for the declared species.",
                                                    "Species positivity and explicit boundary source/sink accounts hold; inadmissible transport rejects the staged update.",
                                                    "Moving sealed barriers, corners, support changes and supported narrow passages preserve side separation and meet approved local transport and forbidden-flux budgets.",
                                                    "Transport composed with two-way passive trajectories preserves ownership and rollback, and retained passive references show no unexplained regression.",
                                                    "Complete transport and combined passive-plus-transport cost, memory and timestep restrictions are measured at approved resolutions; findings do not claim active adoption."
                                                ],
                                                "components": [
                                                    "C-field",
                                                    "C-interface",
                                                    "C-state"
                                                ],
                                                "context": "Proceed only after favorable T-passive-qualification review, not merely report completion. Implement the species portion of AR-work-package using AR-core ownership/staging, AR-field conservative fluxes, AR-geometry side-separated volumes/connectivity, and AR-passive-coupling's moving schedule. Use AR-passive-qualification to retain the reviewed validity range and decisive passive regressions. Keep chambers closed and exclude ports, permeability, reactions, controllers and actuation, which remain downstream. Test stationary advection/diffusion first, then prescribed moving boundaries and two-way passive trajectories. Reuse geometric reference oracles; any earlier fixture-only tracer must remain explicitly nonproduction or be replaced by the production species path in transport integration tests, not become a duplicate solver. Use focused numerical tests and, for temporal behavior, traces and simulation-health capabilities after implementing required telemetry/oracles. Preserve actual configurations, horizons, tolerances, observations and complete incremental/combined cost in supported results.",
                                                "depends_on": [
                                                    "T-core",
                                                    "T-field",
                                                    "T-geometry",
                                                    "T-passive-coupling",
                                                    "T-passive-qualification",
