            "human_decisions": {},
            "plan": "{\n  \"architecture\": {\n    \"components\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-state\",\n        \"name\": \"Authoritative state and advancement\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own stable structural/material references, committed time, inventory ownership, staging, bounded retries, validity checks, and atomic interval acceptance.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-structure\",\n        \"name\": \"Deformable structures\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Represent tissue, membrane edges, area-bearing elements, and contractile attachments; integrate mass, constitutive forces, reactions, and supported contact.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-contents\",\n        \"name\": \"Chamber contents\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own well-mixed enclosed inventories, mass/inertia approximation, geometry-derived pressure and stored energy, and finite exchange ports.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-field\",\n        \"name\": \"Fluid and transported fields\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own environmental liquid, momentum, and species amounts; solve conservative flow and transport with declared outer conditions.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-interface\",\n        \"name\": \"Geometry and conservative coupling\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Derive cut geometry, side-separated membrane barriers, swept volumes, pressure traction, paired impulse/work exchanges, and opening/permeability connectivity.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-biology\",\n        \"name\": \"Local resource processes\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Apply finite transfers, reactions, local sensing, deterministic control, and fuel-limited actuator requests without privileged state edits.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-app\",\n        \"name\": \"Construction and Bitloop shell\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Construct experimental organisms, own engine instances, request fixed simulated intervals, and expose camera, drawing, configuration, replay, and explicit restart adapters.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-evidence\",\n        \"name\": \"Project diagnostics and fixtures\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Provide physical oracles, semantic telemetry, bounded health checks, full-cost benchmarks, inspected snapshots, and reproducible experiment configurations outside the core.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"decisions\": [\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Adopt an evidence-gated foundation project, not an implementation of the entire long-term vision.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-scope\",\n        \"rationale\": \"A small coupled proof must expose unsuitable representations before population complexity or broad biology makes them expensive to replace.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Keep simulation state, constitutive laws, topology, and advancement independent of Scene, UI, rendering, scenario names, trace formats, and file output.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-core\",\n        \"rationale\": \"This preserves ownership, focused testing, and an independently buildable core while reusing Bitloop facilities.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Investigate one CPU candidate: compact connected structures, inertial well-mixed chambers, and conservative cut-cell grid flow with side-separated barriers.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-method\",\n        \"rationale\": \"It directly tests the preferred inexpensive representation without a universal particle solver, backend menu, GPU dependency, or speculative extension framework.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Freeze units, supported geometry, discrete exchange laws, error budgets, solver/retry limits, horizons, and cost accounting before the adoption campaign.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-contract\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Passing global accounts or relaxing tolerances after failure cannot establish correct local behavior.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Use one authoritative committed state with staged updates and bounded failure handling; never skip requested simulated time.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-transaction\",\n        \"rationale\": \"All coupled owners must roll back together, including resources and controller phase, without requiring an unmeasured deep copy at every substep.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Keep physical work, stored energy, physical dissipation, metabolic conversion, and numerical residual separate.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-energy\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Numerical loss must not become heat or fuel, and global corrections must not conceal passive propulsion or local transport errors.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Use only project-owned implementation and public Bitloop facilities; framework or broader dependency changes require explicit user authorization immediately before writing.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-ownership\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Capability declarations neither establish implemented hooks nor authorize changes outside Substrate.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Require a human-approved first work package, favorable prescribed-boundary review before two-way coupling, favorable bounded two-way passive qualification review before full species transport and resource/activity implementation, reviewed representative active coupled adoption evidence, and a separate population screen.\",\n        \"id\": \"D-gates\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Design approval, focused implementation checks, passive feasibility, active numerical adoption, and scale claims are distinct decisions. Completed experiments with negative or inconclusive findings do not release dependent work.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relationships\": [\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-state\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Schedules staged mechanical updates and commits only valid coupled state.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structure\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-state\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Owns transaction boundaries for chamber state and inventory changes.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-contents\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-state\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Coordinates fluid updates, conserved reductions, solver failures, and commit.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-field\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-structure\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Supplies oriented boundary topology, positions, velocities, and material-side identity.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-interface\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-interface\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Supplies fluid-accessible geometry, side connectivity, swept volume, and wall flux constraints; receives pressure and fluid reactions.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-field\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-interface\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Returns paired boundary impulses and measured work using the same geometry as displacement.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structure\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-contents\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Uses actual chamber area and its variation for pressure, wall work, and finite physical ports.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-interface\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-biology\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Submits local sensing-derived transfers and actuator requests through validated staged interfaces.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-state\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-app\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Constructs supported state and requests complete simulated intervals independent of rendering.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-state\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-evidence\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Reads committed-state observations and invokes fixtures without making diagnostics a core dependency.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-state\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-app\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Routes Bitloop headless traces, captures, replay, and checkpoint operations through project-owned adapters.\",\n        \"to\": \"C-evidence\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"summary\": \"One project-owned simulation core maintains authoritative committed state and a bounded transactional advancement schedule. Compact structural mechanics, chamber contents, and fluid control volumes have disjoint ownership of mass and species. A shared geometry/exchange layer makes occupied area, boundary flux, pressure work, and collision barriers agree. Local controllers submit resource-limited requests rather than modifying physical state. A thin Bitloop shell provides construction, presentation, replay, and project-owned diagnostic adapters. Numerical adoption is conditional, not implied by construction.\"\n  },\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Proposed fixture geometry, units, physical scales, references, validity limits, error/cost budgets, horizons, and distinct bounded two-way passive, active prototype adoption, and population-screen protocols, including limits on early tracer/reference probes.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-experiments\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-budgets\",\n      \"title\": \"Bounded experiment and budget specification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Shared data shapes, stable references, units, staged exchange interfaces, ownership rules, and rollback-relevant state.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-state-contract\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-state-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Authoritative state and ownership contract\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Chosen structural discretization, constitutive response, integration and failure limits, attachment interfaces, and worked mechanical references.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-mechanics-design\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-mechanics-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Passive structural mechanics specification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Geometry-derived pressure and energy, contents mass/inertia approximation, wall reactions, finite-port exchange meaning, and worked references.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-contents-design\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-contents-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Inertial chamber specification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Discrete field equations, pressure constraints, species fluxes, outer conditions, convergence limits, geometry interface, and local reference calculations.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-field-design\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-field-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Stationary flow and transport specification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Side-separated cut regions, swept-volume and pressure-work operators, support-change handling, bounded small-cell policy, and geometric reference calculations.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-geometry-design\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-geometry-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Moving geometry and coupling specification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Port/permeability laws, resource ownership transfers, donor limits, competing-request policy, reaction accounts, and worked examples.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-transfer-design\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-transfer-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Finite exchange and reaction specification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Local sensing interface, deterministic cadence, actuator work and fuel law, negative-work policy, rollback behavior, and worked contraction cycle.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-actuation-design\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-actuation-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Local controller and paid-actuation specification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Self-contained implementation contract incorporating the mechanism specifications, coupled schedule, global compatibility, staging/failure semantics, and proposed frozen experiments; its existence does not imply approval.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-work-package\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-schedule-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Reconciled first physical work package\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Implemented authoritative state, stable handles, compact storage, accounts, staging, bounded interval advancement, and focused failure tests.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-core\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-core\",\n      \"title\": \"Transactional simulation core\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Testable tissue/membrane mechanics and boundary/actuator attachment interfaces with focused reference fixtures.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-passive\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-passive\",\n      \"title\": \"Passive structural implementation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Geometry-coupled inertial contents with closed-chamber reference fixtures and explicit supported limits.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-chambers\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-chambers\",\n      \"title\": \"Pressure-bearing chamber implementation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Stationary liquid momentum/pressure solver, conservative face-flux and volume interfaces, outer-boundary material/momentum/work accounts, and focused stationary flow references. Full species transport is a separate implementation deliverable.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-field\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-field\",\n      \"title\": \"Stationary conservative flow implementation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Moving cut geometry, barrier connectivity, swept-volume operators, and independent geometric identity tests.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-geometry\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-geometry\",\n      \"title\": \"Shared geometric operator implementation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Composed moving-boundary field implementation and bounded reference report, including local correctness, convergence, memory, and cost limitations.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-moving-field\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-moving-field\",\n      \"title\": \"Prescribed-boundary fluid package and findings\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Transactional structure–contents–fluid coupling, paired impulse/work exchanges, and passive coupled fixtures.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-passive-coupling\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-passive-coupling\",\n      \"title\": \"Two-way passive coupled implementation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Ports, permeability, reactions, donor-limited paired transfers, and focused conservation and exhaustion tests.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-transfers\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-transfers\",\n      \"title\": \"Finite resource exchange implementation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Local sensing, deterministic control, paid mechanical requests, and loaded-cycle/fuel-exhaustion fixtures.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-actuators\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-actuators\",\n      \"title\": \"Resource-limited controller and actuator implementation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Seeded construction, headless commands, project-owned telemetry, and representative motion, pumping, and resource-limitation examples.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-prototype\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-prototype\",\n      \"title\": \"Runnable active coupled organism\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Predeclared refinement, accumulated-error, behavior, and full-cost campaign findings, including rejection or uncertainty where warranted; not an approval record.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-adoption\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-adoption\",\n      \"title\": \"Representative coupled qualification report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Bounded membrane/terrain contact, friction, narrow-gap compatibility, collision failure policy, worked references, and event-cost limits.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-contact-design\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-contact-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Supported laboratory contact specification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Transactional contact consistent with fluid barriers and a small interacting-organism fixture.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-contact\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-contact\",\n      \"title\": \"Shared-world contact implementation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Reproducible 16-organism fixture and measured active work, complete cost, memory, interaction behavior, and explicit limits on scale/endurance claims.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-population-screen\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-population-screen\",\n      \"title\": \"Interacting laboratory scale-screen report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Thin visual application with pause/step inspection, meaningful overlays, and inspected snapshots correlated with semantic state.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-laboratory\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-presentation\",\n      \"title\": \"Inspectable prototype laboratory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Explicit serialization adapters, continuation-equivalence checks, seeded replay recipe, and complete recording throughput accounting.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-restart\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-restart\",\n      \"title\": \"Restart and recording workflow\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Independent build/run instructions, demonstrations, supported approximation, qualification conclusions, retained counterexamples, and clearly deferred requirements.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-delivery\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-handoff\",\n      \"title\": \"Bounded foundation delivery guide\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Approved passive reference, repeated-cycle and refinement findings; local/cumulative error, rollback, complete cost and memory observations; retained counterexamples, limits and pass/reject/inconclusive conclusions. Not an approval record or species/active/population qualification.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-passive-qualification\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-passive-qualification\",\n      \"title\": \"Bounded two-way passive qualification report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Declared species advection/diffusion using shared flow fluxes and side-separated moving geometry, staged amount ownership and boundary accounts, with stationary and moving/passive reference, positivity, rollback and cost checks. Excludes finite ports, permeability and reactions.\",\n      \"id\": \"AR-species\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-species\",\n      \"title\": \"Conservative species transport implementation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-scope\",\n      \"statement\": \"This initial plan delivers the first coupled proof and a subsequent 16-organism screening fixture, not the complete 256-organism rich world. Damage, repair, reproduction, thermal state, general fracture, automatic representation switching, and evolutionary control are deferred.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-candidate\",\n      \"statement\": \"The provisional candidate is connected deformable structures, well-mixed inertial chambers, and a conservative Cartesian cut-cell fluid/transport field. Its numerical details and suitability require design, human approval, and measured adoption evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-habitat\",\n      \"statement\": \"The initial habitat is completely liquid-filled with declared pressure/open boundaries that can accommodate changing organism area. A sealed incompressible box with independently expanding contents is not assumed physically compatible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-hardware\",\n      \"statement\": \"The Ryzen 9 9950X3D with up to 16 CPU workers is the proposed performance reference. If unavailable, results are diagnostic rather than reference-hardware acceptance unless the user explicitly approves a substitute.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-screen\",\n      \"statement\": \"The proposed 16-organism laboratory target is used only after its geometry, supported interactions, numerical quality, and measurement protocol are approved. A short population screen can reject the candidate but cannot establish rich-world endurance.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The smallest relevant target is built in a Codex-owned context and a real Bitloop headless run identifies the selected scene and fixed-step observations.\",\n        \"The result distinguishes existing hooks from implemented adapters and retains compact evidence under .codex/runs.\",\n        \"Instruction conflicts, unavailable tooling, and external-owner changes are reported rather than bypassed.\",\n        \"The worker publishes its result without attempting to verify its own subsequent persisted completion or review.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-app\",\n        \"C-evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Use capability bitloop, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md; use traces, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md and references/tracing-diagnostics.md under that skill. Identify the active target and exact APIs. Preserve user build state and ownership boundaries D-core/D-ownership. This bounded pilot may add minimal project-owned telemetry, not a diagnostics framework. Record tested claims, source/build identity, actual commands, failed or unverified checks, and substantive observations in supported MindGraph result fields.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Establish the smallest real project-owned build, headless observation, and saved-result handoff without implementing physics.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-bootstrap\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does the pilot expose missing project hooks, ownership conflicts, or evidence-routing failures that prevent the planned supervised workflow?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Run a supervised Bitloop and MindGraph pilot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The persisted and reloaded pilot result contains its actual observations, limitations, and evidence references, and the triggered review is visible.\",\n        \"Missing context, misleading acceptance, instruction conflicts, or evidence loss have minimal reproducers.\",\n        \"Numerical work remains blocked while a consequential workflow failure is unresolved.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"A supervisor or workflow owner examines the completed T-bootstrap result after its review. This is not simulator implementation. Check that substantive observations survive persistence and reload; keep management repairs in their owning project.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-bootstrap\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Verify execution, saved result, review, and reload before substantial numerical work.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-loop-confirm\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Confirm the completed management loop\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The reconciled package contains worked references for all implemented mechanisms and compatible global boundary conditions.\",\n        \"Implementation is released only through the separate human decision task.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-state\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-field\",\n        \"C-interface\",\n        \"C-biology\",\n        \"C-evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Children establish separate physical and numerical contracts, reconcile them, and obtain explicit human approval. A-scope and D-method bound the work.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-loop-confirm\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"group\",\n      \"goal\": \"Resolve the candidate's substantive mechanisms and acceptance policy before implementation.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Establish and approve the bounded numerical work package\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Reference cases cover translation, rotation, pressure equilibrium, free expansion, compression/recovery, advection, diffusion, sealed moving barriers, pumping, and fuel exhaustion.\",\n        \"Local and cumulative error budgets use relevant motion and resource scales, include passive propulsion and weak-motion loss, and specify refinement comparisons.\",\n        \"Campaigns have predeclared time/compute limits, timescale-derived horizons, extension rules, rejection/inconclusive outcomes, and supported event coverage.\",\n        \"The 16-organism proposal preserves up to 128 vertices, two chambers, 16 actuators per organism, 128 by 128 active cells, and the proposed real-time target; exclusions and actual active counts are explicit.\",\n        \"Complete cost includes staging, solves, safety scans, retries, and commit; memory categories, hardware reporting, rendering, recording, and checkpoint accounting are specified.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-evidence\",\n        \"C-app\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Use A-scope/A-hardware/A-screen and D-contract. Define the smallest two-chamber contractile organism that swims and pumps through finite ports, with nutrient exchange and fuel use; it need not represent a named substance. Specify consistent 2D units, shapes, coefficients, minimum features, fixed resolution family, initial conditions, species and energy meanings, and environmental outer conditions. Define prototype and later 16-organism screen separately; do not adopt the 256-organism workload. Numerical tolerances are proposals for human approval, not facts supplied by the vision. Within the prototype protocol, predeclare a bounded two-way passive campaign before species/resource/activity implementation: relevant passive references, repeated externally loaded and unforced cycles, refinement comparisons, local and cumulative errors, rollback injections, full coupled cost, timescale-derived horizons, compute limits, extension rules, and rejection/inconclusive outcomes. Distinguish this campaign from focused coupling tests and later active adoption. Scope any early tracer probe as a geometric/flux reference, not full species-solver qualification.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-loop-confirm\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Turn proposed physical and performance requirements into a bounded, reviewable experimental specification.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-budgets\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Define experiments, validity ranges, and budgets\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Every mass, species amount, momentum contribution, and stored energy has one authoritative owner.\",\n        \"Minimal read views and staged request/result shapes include units, signs, validity conditions, and unsupported-state errors.\",\n        \"A worked ownership example follows a nutrient amount from field through a chamber and reaction without duplicate ownership.\",\n        \"Derived caches and immutable configuration are distinguished from rollback-relevant state.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-state\",\n        \"C-interface\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consume the experiment specification. Define stable handles for structures, chambers, regions and inventories; dense storage is private. Specify positions, velocities, mass, chamber inventories, field amounts, boundary-side identifiers, port endpoints, controller phase, committed time, and observable accounts. Exclude serialization format and universal registries.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-budgets\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Establish minimal core types and ownership boundaries before mechanisms depend on them.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-state-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-experiments\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Define authoritative state and shared data ownership\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Discrete forces or constraints, solver stopping rules, and physical versus numerical dissipation are explicit.\",\n        \"Worked stretch, shear, compression/recovery, rigid translation, and rotation cases establish mass, force, torque, energy, and deformation oracles.\",\n        \"Feature collapse and inversion produce bounded rejection rather than silent deletion or stiffness changes.\",\n        \"Actuator attachment and boundary impulse interfaces are defined without implementing active laws.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Use D-method and the shared state contract. Specify mass allocation, compliant edge/area/shear response, damping, integration, element inversion/degeneracy handling, timestep restrictions, and attachment forces. No population contact, damage, general remeshing, or rigid-region implementation is required here.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-budgets\",\n        \"T-state-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Choose the bounded tissue and membrane discretization with measurable deformation and work error.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-mechanics-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-experiments\",\n        \"AR-state-contract\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Specify passive structural mechanics\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Pressure, stored energy, mass/inertia, concentration, and geometric area use one consistent discrete meaning.\",\n        \"Worked translation, rotation, free expansion, and compression examples show wall reactions and work signs.\",\n        \"Finite inflow/outflow specifies transferred mass, momentum, and energy without invented ejection speed.\",\n        \"Unsupported sloshing, stratification, shape degeneracy, and low-inventory states have explicit detection and failure policies.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-interface\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Define the well-mixed chamber approximation using actual oriented chamber geometry. Choose a bounded inertia model with stated limitations; do not treat contents as massless pressure or double-count them as environmental fluid. Establish compatibility between the chamber pressure law and A-habitat.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-budgets\",\n        \"T-state-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Give cheap contents an honest mechanical meaning separate from tissue mass.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-contents-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-experiments\",\n        \"AR-state-contract\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Specify chamber inertia, pressure, and wall work\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Discrete equations, stored quantities, pressure convergence measures, positivity conditions, and bounded solver work are specified.\",\n        \"Worked stationary pressure, channel flow, uniform advection, and diffusion references establish local as well as global oracles.\",\n        \"Boundary inflow/outflow accounts close material, momentum, species, and work consistently.\",\n        \"The specification defines required geometry inputs and flux outputs, including disconnected fluid regions.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-field\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Choose the discrete incompressible liquid momentum/pressure formulation, viscosity treatment, face fluxes, and conservative advection/diffusion for the declared species. Specify compatible open/pressure outer conditions, pressure null-space treatment where applicable, and initial/boundary data. Keep geometry operators abstract only at the explicit interface consumed by T-geometry-design. Define separate stationary-flow and species-transport implementation boundaries: flow exposes committed/staged conservative fluxes, accessible volumes and boundary accounts without requiring the species solver. Species transport later consumes these interfaces with moving geometry and the qualified passive schedule. Specify any bounded early tracer/reference probe separately from production species transport; it must not establish species positivity, diffusion, or full transport acceptance.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-budgets\",\n        \"T-state-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Define the conservative field solver and species transport before introducing moving geometry.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-field-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-experiments\",\n        \"AR-state-contract\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Specify the stationary fluid and transport equations\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Worked translating/rotating wall, expanding chamber, moving corner, and supported narrow-passage examples establish swept-volume and local transport identities.\",\n        \"Thin barriers prevent interpolation or ordinary cell mixing between opposite sides.\",\n        \"A support-change example shows continuous physical response, including pressure work and remapping error.\",\n        \"Small-cell thresholds, stabilization limits, memory growth, timestep consequences, and unsupported geometry errors are explicit.\",\n        \"The same boundary definition supports later mechanical contact and impermeable field barriers.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-interface\",\n        \"C-field\",\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consume the field equations and boundary state definitions. Specify fluid-accessible subregions, oriented faces, membrane-side connectivity, swept areas, newly uncovered material treatment, and the relationship between divergence and pressure force. Choose one bounded small-cell stabilization strategy that does not merge opposite sides of a membrane.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-budgets\",\n        \"T-state-design\",\n        \"T-field-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Resolve geometric conservation, thin barriers, pressure traction, and small-cell treatment.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-geometry-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-experiments\",\n        \"AR-state-contract\",\n        \"AR-field-design\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Specify moving cut geometry and compatible exchanges\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Worked two-chamber flow and chamber-to-field permeability examples have finite rates, paired inventories, and correct transferred momentum/work where applicable.\",\n        \"Competing drains cannot overspend a donor; exhausted donors and rejected transactions leave no negative or duplicate amounts.\",\n        \"Reaction examples close declared constituent and energy accounts, with explicit waste and sources/sinks.\",\n        \"Connections do not imply instantaneous mixing, and spatial sampling never crosses an intact barrier.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-biology\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-field\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Use declared species, chamber state, and field face/port interfaces. Specify finite channel conductance, permeable flux, local sampling, reaction stoichiometry and rates, donor availability, simultaneous competing requests, and paired recipient updates. No rupture, growth, repair, or thermal conversion is implemented in this scope.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-budgets\",\n        \"T-state-design\",\n        \"T-contents-design\",\n        \"T-field-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Define resource movement and conversion independently of actuation.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-transfer-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-experiments\",\n        \"AR-state-contract\",\n        \"AR-contents-design\",\n        \"AR-field-design\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Specify finite ports, permeability, and reactions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A worked contraction cycle defines force/displacement work signs, available fuel, efficiency, and nonpositive-work policy without generating fuel from numerical residuals.\",\n        \"Fuel exhaustion bounds delivered work and request changes cannot inject unaccounted mechanical energy.\",\n        \"Controller cadence integrates elapsed simulated time and rolls back phase and resource requests on failure.\",\n        \"Local sensing footprint, latency, and gradient validity limits are explicit.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-biology\",\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Define deterministic controller inputs, update cadence, actuator requests, accepted work, and reaction outputs. Use scripted cycles for physical references and a local deterministic controller for the demonstration. Controllers must not set positions, choose solver settings, or read unrestricted world state.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-budgets\",\n        \"T-state-design\",\n        \"T-mechanics-design\",\n        \"T-transfer-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Define how local sensing and finite fuel constrain mechanical activity.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-actuation-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-experiments\",\n        \"AR-state-contract\",\n        \"AR-mechanics-design\",\n        \"AR-transfer-design\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Specify local control and work-limited contraction\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A complete worked substep follows geometry, impulses, pressure work, field fluxes, reactions, fuel, and commit using the mechanism specifications.\",\n        \"A deliberately rejected substep leaves every authoritative owner and actual simulated time unchanged; bounded retry exhaustion returns an actionable failure.\",\n        \"Changing occupied area is compatible with outer flow conditions and chamber compressibility.\",\n        \"The package publishes proposed tolerances, supported resolutions, bounded campaign budgets, and explicit stop conditions without claiming approval.\",\n        \"Unresolved design obligations and expected whole-step cost risks are listed for review.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-state\",\n        \"C-interface\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-field\",\n        \"C-biology\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Reconcile all named design outputs. Specify the coupled substep order, time centering, geometry/pressure/mechanics iteration, conservation reductions, resource reservation and commit order, solver and retry ceilings, and staging cost model. Identify unresolved contradictions rather than silently choosing replacement mechanisms.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-budgets\",\n        \"T-state-design\",\n        \"T-mechanics-design\",\n        \"T-contents-design\",\n        \"T-field-design\",\n        \"T-geometry-design\",\n        \"T-transfer-design\",\n        \"T-actuation-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Assemble the separate mechanisms into one implementable work package without concealing missing laws.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-schedule-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-experiments\",\n        \"AR-state-contract\",\n        \"AR-mechanics-design\",\n        \"AR-contents-design\",\n        \"AR-field-design\",\n        \"AR-geometry-design\",\n        \"AR-transfer-design\",\n        \"AR-actuation-design\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Do the reconciled mechanisms in D-method form a physically compatible and affordable candidate, or do chamber inertia, moving cut geometry, pressure work, or bounded coupling require redesign before approval?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Reconcile coupling, advancement, and failure semantics\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The human explicitly approves or rejects the candidate, validity range, error budgets, performance protocol, compute limits, and bounded scope.\",\n        \"Rejected or unresolved decisions block dependent implementation.\",\n        \"No tolerance is weakened implicitly in response to a future failing campaign.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Present AR-work-package after the T-schedule-design review. Approval is a workflow decision, not an artifact inferred from the package's existence. Any requested physical or budget change must update the affected design before release.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"human_decision\",\n      \"goal\": \"Release implementation only after explicit approval of scope, approximation, budgets, and experiments.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-approve\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Obtain human approval of the first physical work package\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Independent mechanism tests and a reproducible active coupled fixture exist.\",\n        \"No mechanism silently departs from the approved physical contract.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-state\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-field\",\n        \"C-interface\",\n        \"C-biology\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Children implement D-core/D-transaction within the approved work package. No later population, damage, repair, checkpoint, or presentation work is necessary to reach the first coupled result.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-approve\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"group\",\n      \"goal\": \"Implement the approved candidate as focused packages before active-organism adoption.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Build the independently testable coupled foundation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A focused target exercises commit, rejection, retry exhaustion, stale references, nonfinite values, and requested-versus-actual simulated time.\",\n        \"Injected failure preserves all staged-owner state and committed time.\",\n        \"Empty and representative-size staging cost and memory are measured rather than assumed negligible.\",\n        \"The implemented core API is available to downstream mechanism packages.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-state\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Implement the state and advancement portions of AR-work-package, including stable handles, compact storage, immutable configuration, scratch reuse, interval result/error types, and conserved accounts. Use bitloop capability via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md for public math and CMake integration only; keep the core independent of framework lifecycle and diagnostics.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-approve\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Provide the core state, staging, time, and exchange interfaces consumed by all mechanisms.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-core\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement authoritative state and bounded transactions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Stretch, shear, compression/recovery, translation, and rotation meet approved force, torque, deformation, and energy-error criteria.\",\n        \"Resolution/timestep comparisons expose damping and integration error.\",\n        \"Degenerate or inverted features reject safely without deleting material.\",\n        \"Focused tests retain physical versus numerical work observations.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Implement the approved structural law and attachment interfaces using AR-core. Keep active actuation and population contact out of this task.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-core\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver passive mechanical response independently of chambers or fluid.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-passive\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-core\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement passive tissue and membrane mechanics\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Translation and rotation include contents mass/inertia exactly as specified, without duplication.\",\n        \"Pressure equilibrium, free expansion, and compression/recovery meet local geometry, pressure, and wall-work budgets.\",\n        \"Low-inventory and invalid-geometry cases follow the approved failure policy.\",\n        \"A closed chamber trajectory demonstrates bounded cumulative error over the specified passive horizon.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Implement the approved contents model using AR-passive and AR-core. Keep ports closed for these references; fluid-field coupling and reaction laws remain separate.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-core\",\n        \"T-passive\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Add geometry-based chamber contents and wall reactions on passive structures.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-chambers\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-core\",\n        \"AR-passive\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement inertial pressure chambers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Stationary pressure and channel flow meet approved local-field and global-balance references.\",\n        \"Fluid material, momentum, and work accounts include explicit outer-boundary sources and sinks; exported fluxes and volumes meet the approved interface contract.\",\n        \"Pressure convergence, iteration ceilings, memory, and complete field-step cost are recorded at prescribed resolutions.\",\n        \"Unconverged pressure and inadmissible flow reject the staged update.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-field\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Implement the approved stationary liquid momentum/pressure equations on AR-core with prescribed static geometry and pressure/open boundaries. Expose conservative face fluxes, accessible volumes, and staged boundary accounts for moving geometry and later species transport. Use the reconciled AR-work-package, including its field specification. Full species advection/diffusion belongs to T-species; chamber transfers and reactions remain separate.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-core\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Establish stationary flow correctness, conservative flux interfaces, and pressure cost before moving boundaries.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-field\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-core\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement stationary conservative fluid flow\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Analytic swept-area tests for translation, rotation, expansion, and moving corners meet local and global tolerances.\",\n        \"Membrane sides remain disconnected, including same-cell intersections and supported narrow passages.\",\n        \"Support changes and small-cell stabilization preserve approved conservation identities without merging incompatible regions.\",\n        \"Unsupported geometric features fail explicitly and operator memory/work are measured.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-interface\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Implement the geometry portion of AR-work-package using AR-core. Do not bury geometry validation inside a fluid trajectory. Tests may prescribe boundary paths analytically.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-core\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Provide independently testable conservative geometry and barrier connectivity.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-geometry\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-core\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement shared moving-geometry operators\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Uniform-pressure equilibrium, free expansion, sealed moving barriers, moving corners, and support changes are tested across approved refinements.\",\n        \"Local displaced volume, wall flux and wall work are checked independently of global balances; any bounded tracer/reference probe records its scope and limitations and is not full species-transport qualification.\",\n        \"Timestep, pressure convergence, small-cell work, memory, and complete prescribed-boundary cost are reported against approved limits.\",\n        \"The report identifies failed, passed, and inconclusive conditions and does not equate experiment completion with adoption.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-field\",\n        \"C-interface\",\n        \"C-evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Compose AR-field and AR-geometry with analytic boundary trajectories. Use simulation-health capability, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md for approved horizons and temporary probes; project oracles must be implemented. Test local displaced volume, wall flux and pressure work directly. Where the approved references require tagged transport, use a bounded fixture-only tracer/reference probe over the actual geometric and flow fluxes, not a second production transport path. It must neither require T-species nor claim full species-solver acceptance. Retain negative or inconclusive outcomes as valid experiment results.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-field\",\n        \"T-geometry\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Test moving-wall displacement and pressure work without two-way mechanical feedback.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-moving-field\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-field\",\n        \"AR-geometry\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does prescribed-boundary evidence support D-method's cut-cell/barrier treatment at the approved quality and cost, or must geometry/pressure coupling change before two-way reliance?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Qualify prescribed-boundary fluid response\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Passive equilibrium, translation/rotation, compression/recovery, and expansion satisfy local fields, momentum reactions, and approved work budgets.\",\n        \"Closed unforced cycles show no sustained unexplained energy growth or passive propulsion.\",\n        \"Injected coupling failure rolls back mechanics, contents, geometry-dependent state, fluid, and time together.\",\n        \"Complete coupled step cost includes staging, geometry, pressure iterations, safety checks, and rejected attempts.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-state\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-field\",\n        \"C-interface\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Proceed only after favorable review of AR-moving-field. Implement the approved coupling schedule and paired impulse/work interfaces; keep ports closed and omit active biology and full species transport. Use simulation-health via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md under .agents/skills/bitloop-development. This task delivers focused passive integration, rollback, and cost checks; T-passive-qualification separately evaluates repeated-cycle/refinement feasibility before downstream species/resource/activity work.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-core\",\n        \"T-passive\",\n        \"T-chambers\",\n        \"T-moving-field\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Join passive structures, inertial contents, and environmental fluid with transactional reactions.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-passive-coupling\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-core\",\n        \"AR-passive\",\n        \"AR-chambers\",\n        \"AR-moving-field\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement two-way passive chamber–fluid coupling\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Two-chamber transport has measured finite equilibration rather than instant mixing.\",\n        \"Permeability and real openings exchange paired species, mass, momentum, and work as specified, while sealed boundaries have forbidden flux below budget.\",\n        \"Competing donor requests, exhaustion, and rejected transactions preserve positivity and ownership.\",\n        \"Reaction tests close declared constituent and energy accounts and retain explicit waste/source/sink observations.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-biology\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-field\",\n        \"C-interface\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Proceed only after favorable T-passive-qualification review and completion of T-species. Implement the transfer/reaction portion of AR-work-package against field, species, chamber and geometry interfaces. Use AR-passive-qualification's supported limits; its existence alone is not approval. Exercise static or prescribed geometry first, then verify paired transfers through the established moving/passive schedule using AR-species. Exclude rupture, growth, repair and heat.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-core\",\n        \"T-chambers\",\n        \"T-field\",\n        \"T-geometry\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\",\n        \"T-passive-qualification\",\n        \"T-species\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver conservative ports, permeability, and resource conversion independently of active mechanics.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-transfers\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-core\",\n        \"AR-chambers\",\n        \"AR-field\",\n        \"AR-geometry\",\n        \"AR-work-package\",\n        \"AR-passive-qualification\",\n        \"AR-species\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement finite exchange and local reactions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A loaded actuator cycle demonstrates the approved relationship between fuel expenditure and accepted work.\",\n        \"Fuel exhaustion limits contraction, negative-work handling matches policy, and numerical residual cannot fund activity.\",\n        \"Controller reads remain local and requests cannot teleport inventory or edit physical state.\",\n        \"Replay and forced-rejection tests preserve controller cadence, resource reservations, and deterministic behavior.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-biology\",\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Implement the approved local controller and actuator law using AR-transfers and AR-passive. Test scripted cycles and deterministic local feedback; no organism-specific swimming physics or general brain framework.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-core\",\n        \"T-passive\",\n        \"T-transfers\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Connect bounded controller requests to paid mechanical work.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-actuators\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-core\",\n        \"AR-passive\",\n        \"AR-transfers\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement local sensing and fuel-limited actuation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A documented headless command runs the seeded approved fixture for fixed simulated intervals independent of rendering.\",\n        \"Semantic traces expose inventories, local fluxes, chamber pressure/area, actuator fuel/work, motion, pressure iterations, retries, and actual committed time.\",\n        \"Focused integration cases show pumping against load, nutrient uptake, useful motion, and loss of actuation when fuel is exhausted.\",\n        \"A smoke run is explicitly labeled integration evidence, not adoption or endurance.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-app\",\n        \"C-evidence\",\n        \"C-biology\",\n        \"C-state\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Compose AR-passive-coupling, AR-species, AR-transfers, and AR-actuators using the approved fixture after the favorable passive qualification gate. Use bitloop and traces capabilities via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md and its references/tracing-diagnostics.md. Keep Substrate/Substrate.h and .cpp thin; place construction and telemetry outside core ownership. Passive qualification and focused transport checks do not replace T-adoption's later active coupled campaign.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-passive-coupling\",\n        \"T-transfers\",\n        \"T-actuators\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\",\n        \"T-species\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver the smallest runnable organism demonstrating motion, pumping, nutrient exchange, and fuel limitation.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-prototype\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-passive-coupling\",\n        \"AR-transfers\",\n        \"AR-actuators\",\n        \"AR-work-package\",\n        \"AR-species\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Construct the first active coupled organism\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The report compares approved resolutions/timesteps at equal simulated duration, including local transport, pressure, shape, motion, pumping work, gradients, and resource affordability.\",\n        \"Hard monitors run throughout; selected full committed-state inspections and anomaly-local probes cover relaxation, transport, forcing, and accumulation timescales.\",\n        \"Complete cost and memory include all substeps, rejected attempts, staging, coupling solves, and safety work, with actual hardware/build/precision/worker details.\",\n        \"Passive propulsion, cyclic gain, lost weak motion, feature collapse, and unresolved drift are explicitly assessed against predeclared budgets.\",\n        \"Failed or inconclusive results are retained with counterexamples; reaching the experiment's budget is not recorded as physical adoption.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-evidence\",\n        \"C-state\",\n        \"C-interface\",\n        \"C-biology\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Use AR-prototype and the frozen AR-work-package without weakening limits. Use traces and simulation-health via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md, and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/tracing-diagnostics.md and simulation-health-diagnostics.md. Run bounded refinement and repeated-cycle comparisons before population expansion. Numerical conclusions must be retained in supported result fields as well as the report.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-prototype\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Determine whether the candidate preserves meaningful behavior and complete cost over approved horizons and refinements.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-adoption\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-prototype\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does AR-adoption justify adopting the representative coupled candidate under D-contract/D-energy, or do behavior, accumulated local error, or full cost require rejection before contact and population expansion?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Run the representative coupled adoption campaign\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Worked two-body and body–terrain contacts establish momentum, reaction, friction work, and penetration tolerances.\",\n        \"Fluid-gap closure and under-resolved passages have explicit supported limits and failure semantics, with no erased walls or mixed chamber contents.\",\n        \"Contact candidate counts, iteration/retry limits, and event-burst cost budgets are defined before implementation.\",\n        \"Any contact law that materially changes the approved physical approximation is returned for human decision rather than silently adopted.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-interface\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Proceed only after favorable T-adoption review. Specify broad phase, deformable membrane/terrain contact, self-contact policy, friction, impulses/work, collision time handling, narrow-gap validity, and compatibility with fluid barriers. Scope is the approved laboratory screen, not general fracture or arbitrary dense packing.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-adoption\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Establish a bounded contact model only after the coupled foundation merits expansion.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-contact-design\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-adoption\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Define supported population contact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Two-body, terrain, friction, self-contact-policy, and narrow-gap tests satisfy the contact contract.\",\n        \"Contact and field barriers agree during moving collisions with no forbidden inventory passage.\",\n        \"Forced collision failure rolls back the complete state and time.\",\n        \"A small interacting fixture records contact work, candidate counts, retries, and event-burst cost.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-interface\",\n        \"C-state\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Implement AR-contact-design on AR-prototype, reusing shared boundary geometry. Contact must participate in the same transaction and full-cost accounts; do not introduce a separate physics world.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-contact-design\",\n        \"T-prototype\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Enable organisms to interact mechanically with each other and terrain in the supported habitat.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-contact\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-contact-design\",\n        \"AR-prototype\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement bounded shared-world contact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The reproducible fixture reports actual vertices, bonds/elements, chambers, actuators, active cells, species, controller work, and event rates rather than organism count alone.\",\n        \"Whole calculated intervals include every substep and retry; throughput, latency distribution, maximum latency, pressure work, and memory are reported on the declared machine.\",\n        \"The proposed one simulated second per wall-clock second target is evaluated at the approved quality without sleeping away biological activity.\",\n        \"Repeated windows include interactions and event bursts; negative or inconclusive evidence stops scale expansion.\",\n        \"The report explicitly states that this screen does not prove the 256-organism target or ten-minute/100-cycle rich-world endurance.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-app\",\n        \"C-evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Proceed only on favorable T-adoption review and within the frozen laboratory protocol. Use AR-contact and AR-work-package. Use traces and simulation-health via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and the corresponding tracing-diagnostics.md and simulation-health-diagnostics.md references under .agents/skills/bitloop-development. All organisms sense, metabolize, and actuate; shared flow, contact, pumping, feeding, and resource competition must be active.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-adoption\",\n        \"T-contact\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Expose whole-world cost and interaction failures without claiming rich-world acceptance.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-population-screen\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-adoption\",\n        \"AR-contact\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does the interacting 16-organism screen support affordable scaling of the adopted foundation, or do shared pressure, contact, safety/staging, and transport costs invalidate A-screen and require a new representation decision?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Run the separate 16-organism scale screen\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A human can launch, pause, single-step, and inspect the representative organism with declared units and actual simulated time.\",\n        \"Drawing shows structure, chamber boundaries, relevant flow/species fields, and fuel/work observations without changing authoritative state.\",\n        \"Inspected snapshots correlate with semantic state and show distinguishable healthy, depleted, and stopped-error states.\",\n        \"Rendering cost is measured separately and the run remains independent of render cadence.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-app\",\n        \"C-evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Proceed after favorable T-adoption review; this work need not wait for the population screen. Use bitloop and snapshots-checkpoints capabilities via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/snapshots-checkpoints.md, .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md and references/checkpoints-snapshots.md and visual-qa.md. Capture support must be checked; this task does not implement checkpoint serialization.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-adoption\",\n        \"T-prototype\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Expose the accepted prototype through a thin visual shell without making rendering part of the physics.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-presentation\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-adoption\",\n        \"AR-prototype\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Deliver an inspectable prototype laboratory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Explicit save/load rejects incompatible or malformed checkpoints without modifying valid running state.\",\n        \"Uninterrupted and save/restore continuations agree by declared fingerprints or approved tolerances, including resource/work accounts and controller phase.\",\n        \"Seeded replay repeats accepted behavior on the declared configuration.\",\n        \"A recording command reports physics, rendering, capture/checkpoint I/O, and total user-facing throughput separately.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-app\",\n        \"C-state\",\n        \"C-evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Proceed after favorable T-adoption review. Use snapshots-checkpoints and traces via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/snapshots-checkpoints.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/checkpoints-snapshots.md and tracing-diagnostics.md. Generated checkpoint hooks are not assumed implemented. Serialize authoritative state, controller/RNG state, configuration identity and actual time; rebuild derived caches. No cross-hardware bitwise promise.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-adoption\",\n        \"T-core\",\n        \"T-prototype\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Make accepted prototype experiments restartable and recordable on a declared execution configuration.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-restart\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-adoption\",\n        \"AR-core\",\n        \"AR-prototype\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement explicit restart and reproducible recordings\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A clean-clone build/run recipe identifies required dependencies, representative commands, supported configuration, and ownership boundaries.\",\n        \"The final guide distinguishes physical adoption, scale-screen results, visual evidence, and restart equivalence.\",\n        \"Limits, unresolved drift/cost risks, deferred rich-world requirements, and negative outcomes are plainly stated.\",\n        \"Superseded candidate code and disposable probes are removed only after useful counterexamples and compact findings are preserved.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-app\",\n        \"C-evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Integrate presentation, restart, and population-screen findings without new physical mechanisms. If a review rejects the foundation, publish the negative findings and do not label it adopted. Reuse the existing project documentation rather than creating a competing roadmap.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-presentation\",\n        \"T-restart\",\n        \"T-population-screen\",\n        \"T-adoption\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver runnable examples, qualification conclusions, and an honest statement of what remains unproven.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-handoff\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-laboratory\",\n        \"AR-restart\",\n        \"AR-population-screen\",\n        \"AR-adoption\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Publish the bounded foundation and its limits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The approved passive references and repeated-cycle/refinement comparisons are executed or explicitly reported unverified, with local and cumulative errors compared against the frozen budgets.\",\n        \"Hard monitors and selected complete committed-state inspections cover declared relaxation, forcing and accumulation timescales; horizons, extension/stopping rationale and unresolved drift are recorded.\",\n        \"Injected failures and retry exhaustion report preservation of all authoritative passive owners and committed time, with requested versus actual simulated intervals.\",\n        \"Complete interval cost and memory include staging, geometry, mechanics, contents, pressure/coupling iterations, safety work, rejected attempts and commit; hardware, build, precision and workers are recorded under A-hardware.\",\n        \"The report retains decisive configurations and counterexamples, distinguishes pass/reject/inconclusive findings from experiment completion, and states that species, active behavior and population suitability remain unqualified.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-evidence\",\n        \"C-state\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-field\",\n        \"C-interface\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consume AR-passive-coupling and the human-approved AR-work-package. Run its bounded passive campaign with closed ports and no metabolism, controller, actuator, or full species solver. Cover equilibrium, translation/rotation, free expansion, compression/recovery, moving barriers/corners, supported narrow passages and support changes as specified. Use externally applied loads with explicit work accounts for repeated compression cycles and separate closed unforced cases. Compare approved resolutions/timesteps at equal simulated durations; assess local geometry/volume, pressure, shape, reactions, wall work, weak-motion loss, passive propulsion, cyclic gain and accumulated drift. Inject coupling failures and exercise bounded retry exhaustion. Use simulation-health and traces capabilities with implemented project oracles and telemetry, controlled configurations, meaningful scales and justified horizons; record actual commands, source/build/hardware identity, observations, tolerances and limits in supported MindGraph result fields. Preserve compact findings under .codex/runs. Do not weaken approved limits or claim active/population adoption. A negative or inconclusive completed campaign blocks downstream reliance pending review.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-passive-coupling\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Determine whether two-way structure–contents–fluid behavior and complete cost justify species and resource/activity implementation.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-passive-qualification\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-passive-coupling\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does the bounded two-way passive campaign support the candidate's local behavior, accumulated error and complete cost, or must the foundation change before species transport and resource/activity implementation?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Qualify the two-way passive foundation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Uniform advection and diffusion satisfy approved local concentration/profile, global amount and refinement references for the declared species.\",\n        \"Species positivity and explicit boundary source/sink accounts hold; inadmissible transport rejects the staged update.\",\n        \"Moving sealed barriers, corners, support changes and supported narrow passages preserve side separation and meet approved local transport and forbidden-flux budgets.\",\n        \"Transport composed with two-way passive trajectories preserves ownership and rollback, and retained passive references show no unexplained regression.\",\n        \"Complete transport and combined passive-plus-transport cost, memory and timestep restrictions are measured at approved resolutions; findings do not claim active adoption.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-field\",\n        \"C-interface\",\n        \"C-state\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Proceed only after favorable T-passive-qualification review, not merely report completion. Implement the species portion of AR-work-package using AR-core ownership/staging, AR-field conservative fluxes, AR-geometry side-separated volumes/connectivity, and AR-passive-coupling's moving schedule. Use AR-passive-qualification to retain the reviewed validity range and decisive passive regressions. Keep chambers closed and exclude ports, permeability, reactions, controllers and actuation, which remain downstream. Test stationary advection/diffusion first, then prescribed moving boundaries and two-way passive trajectories. Reuse geometric reference oracles; any earlier fixture-only tracer must remain explicitly nonproduction or be replaced by the production species path in transport integration tests, not become a duplicate solver. Use focused numerical tests and, for temporal behavior, traces and simulation-health capabilities after implementing required telemetry/oracles. Preserve actual configurations, horizons, tolerances, observations and complete incremental/combined cost in supported results.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"T-core\",\n        \"T-field\",\n        \"T-geometry\",\n        \"T-passive-coupling\",\n        \"T-passive-qualification\",\n        \"T-schedule-design\"\n      ],\n      \"execution_kind\": \"work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver declared species advection/diffusion with positivity, local accuracy and barrier preservation before finite resource exchange.\",\n      \"id\": \"T-species\",\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\n        \"AR-core\",\n        \"AR-field\",\n        \"AR-geometry\",\n        \"AR-passive-coupling\",\n        \"AR-passive-qualification\",\n        \"AR-work-package\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement conservative species transport on the qualified foundation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"vision_summary\": \"Establish an independently runnable Substrate foundation through an approved, bounded coupled-organism experiment: deformable tissue, honest pressure-bearing contents, moving-boundary environmental flow, nutrient transport, and fuel-limited actuation. Qualify physical behavior, accumulated error, and complete cost before a separate interacting-population rejection screen. The rich world, evolution, and broader material features remain later scope.\"\n}",
