            "previous_reviews": [],
            "question": "Refine this freshly generated plan before any implementation is run. The user authorized repeated planning from VISION.md and quality improvements, while requiring a task DAG at least as good as the backed-up plan. This is a planning-quality assessment, not numerical evidence or approval of a solver.\n\nThe task/artifact model is coherent, but two related work-package/sequencing weaknesses remain:\n1. T-passive-coupling implements the first two-way foundation and performs focused checks, yet it has no separate bounded passive qualification campaign or review gate. T-transfers and T-actuators can be implemented before that foundation is accepted; the only two-way adoption campaign, T-adoption, happens after constructing the whole active prototype. Preserve the backed-up plan's useful early passive feasibility decision by inserting a bounded passive campaign after T-passive-coupling and before substantial dependent resource/activity work. Cover relevant physical references, repeated cycles/refinement, local error, rollback and complete coupled cost using already approved budgets. Keep negative/inconclusive findings distinct from completion and retain T-adoption's later active proof plus the separate population review. This is not a request to invent results or new numerical tolerances.\n2. T-field currently combines stationary fluid implementation and species transport; make their independently testable work explicit. Establish stationary flow before prescribed-boundary/two-way passive work, then establish conservative species transport against the qualified moving/passive foundation before transfers and actuation. Keep their design prerequisites sufficient and don't make stationary moving-boundary tests require an as-yet-unimplemented full species solver. A bounded tracer/reference probe can be scoped explicitly if needed for a moving-geometry test.\n\nMake the smallest coherent plan edits that resolve these weaknesses. Preserve the successful bootstrap/supervisor separation, design reconciliation and distinct human approval, core ownership, deferred broader scope and other unaffected tasks. Preserve stable IDs for continuing work. Update affected task contexts, criteria, dependencies, artifact descriptions/references, and the gate decision together. Keep new design/implementation/evidence artifacts distinct; reuse the same artifact ID for shared consumers. All tasks are unrun, so this request justifies plan edits, not implementation repairs or claims of failed code. Return a concrete propose_changes response if warranted under the existing reviewer schema.",
            "raw_response": "{\n  \"base_revision\": 1,\n  \"outcome\": \"propose_changes\",\n  \"reason\": \"The requested sequencing improvements are justified by the unrun DAG: two-way passive feasibility should be reviewed before resource/activity implementation, and stationary flow should not depend on full species transport. Preserve the later active adoption and population gates; no implementation repairs or numerical conclusions are warranted.\",\n  \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Make the early passive decision explicit without replacing human approval or later qualification.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"decision\", \"id\": \"D-gates\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"decision\",\n            \"value\": \"Require a human-approved first work package, favorable prescribed-boundary review before two-way coupling, favorable bounded two-way passive qualification review before full species transport and resource/activity implementation, reviewed representative active coupled adoption evidence, and a separate population screen.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"rationale\",\n            \"value\": \"Design approval, focused implementation checks, passive feasibility, active numerical adoption, and scale claims are distinct decisions. Completed experiments with negative or inconclusive findings do not release dependent work.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Define the early campaign within the existing budget and approval process rather than inventing thresholds later.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-budgets\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Use A-scope/A-hardware/A-screen and D-contract. Define the smallest two-chamber contractile organism that swims and pumps through finite ports, with nutrient exchange and fuel use; it need not represent a named substance. Specify consistent 2D units, shapes, coefficients, minimum features, fixed resolution family, initial conditions, species and energy meanings, and environmental outer conditions. Define prototype and later 16-organism screen separately; do not adopt the 256-organism workload. Numerical tolerances are proposals for human approval, not facts supplied by the vision. Within the prototype protocol, predeclare a bounded two-way passive campaign before species/resource/activity implementation: relevant passive references, repeated externally loaded and unforced cycles, refinement comparisons, local and cumulative errors, rollback injections, full coupled cost, timescale-derived horizons, compute limits, extension rules, and rejection/inconclusive outcomes. Distinguish this campaign from focused coupling tests and later active adoption. Scope any early tracer probe as a geometric/flux reference, not full species-solver qualification.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Expose the passive campaign in the shared experiment contract consumed by design reconciliation.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"artifact\", \"id\": \"AR-experiments\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"description\",\n            \"value\": \"Proposed fixture geometry, units, physical scales, references, validity limits, error/cost budgets, horizons, and distinct bounded two-way passive, active prototype adoption, and population-screen protocols, including limits on early tracer/reference probes.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Keep the shared field design sufficient for both implementation stages and their interface.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-field-design\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Choose the discrete incompressible liquid momentum/pressure formulation, viscosity treatment, face fluxes, and conservative advection/diffusion for the declared species. Specify compatible open/pressure outer conditions, pressure null-space treatment where applicable, and initial/boundary data. Keep geometry operators abstract only at the explicit interface consumed by T-geometry-design. Define separate stationary-flow and species-transport implementation boundaries: flow exposes committed/staged conservative fluxes, accessible volumes and boundary accounts without requiring the species solver. Species transport later consumes these interfaces with moving geometry and the qualified passive schedule. Specify any bounded early tracer/reference probe separately from production species transport; it must not establish species positivity, diffusion, or full transport acceptance.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Retain T-field for the continuing stationary-flow outcome and move full species implementation into distinct work.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-field\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\"field\": \"title\", \"value\": \"Implement stationary conservative fluid flow\"},\n          {\n            \"field\": \"goal\",\n            \"value\": \"Establish stationary flow correctness, conservative flux interfaces, and pressure cost before moving boundaries.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Implement the approved stationary liquid momentum/pressure equations on AR-core with prescribed static geometry and pressure/open boundaries. Expose conservative face fluxes, accessible volumes, and staged boundary accounts for moving geometry and later species transport. Use the reconciled AR-work-package, including its field specification. Full species advection/diffusion belongs to T-species; chamber transfers and reactions remain separate.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n            \"value\": [\n              \"Stationary pressure and channel flow meet approved local-field and global-balance references.\",\n              \"Fluid material, momentum, and work accounts include explicit outer-boundary sources and sinks; exported fluxes and volumes meet the approved interface contract.\",\n              \"Pressure convergence, iteration ceilings, memory, and complete field-step cost are recorded at prescribed resolutions.\",\n              \"Unconverged pressure and inadmissible flow reject the staged update.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Keep the continuing flow artifact accurate after extracting species implementation.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"artifact\", \"id\": \"AR-field\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\"field\": \"title\", \"value\": \"Stationary conservative flow implementation\"},\n          {\n            \"field\": \"description\",\n            \"value\": \"Stationary liquid momentum/pressure solver, conservative face-flux and volume interfaces, outer-boundary material/momentum/work accounts, and focused stationary flow references. Full species transport is a separate implementation deliverable.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Preserve early local transport diagnostics without requiring the deferred species solver.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-moving-field\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Compose AR-field and AR-geometry with analytic boundary trajectories. Use simulation-health capability, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md for approved horizons and temporary probes; project oracles must be implemented. Test local displaced volume, wall flux and pressure work directly. Where the approved references require tagged transport, use a bounded fixture-only tracer/reference probe over the actual geometric and flow fluxes, not a second production transport path. It must neither require T-species nor claim full species-solver acceptance. Retain negative or inconclusive outcomes as valid experiment results.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n            \"value\": [\n              \"Uniform-pressure equilibrium, free expansion, sealed moving barriers, moving corners, and support changes are tested across approved refinements.\",\n              \"Local displaced volume, wall flux and wall work are checked independently of global balances; any bounded tracer/reference probe records its scope and limitations and is not full species-transport qualification.\",\n              \"Timestep, pressure convergence, small-cell work, memory, and complete prescribed-boundary cost are reported against approved limits.\",\n              \"The report identifies failed, passed, and inconclusive conditions and does not equate experiment completion with adoption.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Keep coupling implementation and its focused tests distinct from the new qualification campaign.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-passive-coupling\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Proceed only after favorable review of AR-moving-field. Implement the approved coupling schedule and paired impulse/work interfaces; keep ports closed and omit active biology and full species transport. Use simulation-health via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md under .agents/skills/bitloop-development. This task delivers focused passive integration, rollback, and cost checks; T-passive-qualification separately evaluates repeated-cycle/refinement feasibility before downstream species/resource/activity work.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Insert the requested bounded early evidence gate after implementation and before substantial downstream reliance.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"add_task\",\n        \"task\": {\n          \"id\": \"T-passive-qualification\",\n          \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n          \"title\": \"Qualify the two-way passive foundation\",\n          \"goal\": \"Determine whether two-way structure–contents–fluid behavior and complete cost justify species and resource/activity implementation.\",\n          \"context\": \"Consume AR-passive-coupling and the human-approved AR-work-package. Run its bounded passive campaign with closed ports and no metabolism, controller, actuator, or full species solver. Cover equilibrium, translation/rotation, free expansion, compression/recovery, moving barriers/corners, supported narrow passages and support changes as specified. Use externally applied loads with explicit work accounts for repeated compression cycles and separate closed unforced cases. Compare approved resolutions/timesteps at equal simulated durations; assess local geometry/volume, pressure, shape, reactions, wall work, weak-motion loss, passive propulsion, cyclic gain and accumulated drift. Inject coupling failures and exercise bounded retry exhaustion. Use simulation-health and traces capabilities with implemented project oracles and telemetry, controlled configurations, meaningful scales and justified horizons; record actual commands, source/build/hardware identity, observations, tolerances and limits in supported MindGraph result fields. Preserve compact findings under .codex/runs. Do not weaken approved limits or claim active/population adoption. A negative or inconclusive completed campaign blocks downstream reliance pending review.\",\n          \"components\": [\"C-evidence\", \"C-state\", \"C-structure\", \"C-contents\", \"C-field\", \"C-interface\"],\n          \"depends_on\": [\"T-passive-coupling\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n          \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n            \"The approved passive references and repeated-cycle/refinement comparisons are executed or explicitly reported unverified, with local and cumulative errors compared against the frozen budgets.\",\n            \"Hard monitors and selected complete committed-state inspections cover declared relaxation, forcing and accumulation timescales; horizons, extension/stopping rationale and unresolved drift are recorded.\",\n            \"Injected failures and retry exhaustion report preservation of all authoritative passive owners and committed time, with requested versus actual simulated intervals.\",\n            \"Complete interval cost and memory include staging, geometry, mechanics, contents, pressure/coupling iterations, safety work, rejected attempts and commit; hardware, build, precision and workers are recorded under A-hardware.\",\n            \"The report retains decisive configurations and counterexamples, distinguishes pass/reject/inconclusive findings from experiment completion, and states that species, active behavior and population suitability remain unqualified.\"\n          ],\n          \"plan_review\": {\n            \"question\": \"Does the bounded two-way passive campaign support the candidate's local behavior, accumulated error and complete cost, or must the foundation change before species transport and resource/activity implementation?\"\n          },\n          \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-passive-coupling\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Keep qualification evidence distinct from passive implementation and approval state.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"add_artifact\",\n        \"artifact\": {\n          \"id\": \"AR-passive-qualification\",\n          \"title\": \"Bounded two-way passive qualification report\",\n          \"description\": \"Approved passive reference, repeated-cycle and refinement findings; local/cumulative error, rollback, complete cost and memory observations; retained counterexamples, limits and pass/reject/inconclusive conclusions. Not an approval record or species/active/population qualification.\",\n          \"produced_by\": \"T-passive-qualification\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Make species transport independently testable against the reviewed moving/passive foundation.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"add_task\",\n        \"task\": {\n          \"id\": \"T-species\",\n          \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n          \"title\": \"Implement conservative species transport on the qualified foundation\",\n          \"goal\": \"Deliver declared species advection/diffusion with positivity, local accuracy and barrier preservation before finite resource exchange.\",\n          \"context\": \"Proceed only after favorable T-passive-qualification review, not merely report completion. Implement the species portion of AR-work-package using AR-core ownership/staging, AR-field conservative fluxes, AR-geometry side-separated volumes/connectivity, and AR-passive-coupling's moving schedule. Use AR-passive-qualification to retain the reviewed validity range and decisive passive regressions. Keep chambers closed and exclude ports, permeability, reactions, controllers and actuation, which remain downstream. Test stationary advection/diffusion first, then prescribed moving boundaries and two-way passive trajectories. Reuse geometric reference oracles; any earlier fixture-only tracer must remain explicitly nonproduction or be replaced by the production species path in transport integration tests, not become a duplicate solver. Use focused numerical tests and, for temporal behavior, traces and simulation-health capabilities after implementing required telemetry/oracles. Preserve actual configurations, horizons, tolerances, observations and complete incremental/combined cost in supported results.\",\n          \"components\": [\"C-field\", \"C-interface\", \"C-state\"],\n          \"depends_on\": [\"T-core\", \"T-field\", \"T-geometry\", \"T-passive-coupling\", \"T-passive-qualification\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n          \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n            \"Uniform advection and diffusion satisfy approved local concentration/profile, global amount and refinement references for the declared species.\",\n            \"Species positivity and explicit boundary source/sink accounts hold; inadmissible transport rejects the staged update.\",\n            \"Moving sealed barriers, corners, support changes and supported narrow passages preserve side separation and meet approved local transport and forbidden-flux budgets.\",\n            \"Transport composed with two-way passive trajectories preserves ownership and rollback, and retained passive references show no unexplained regression.\",\n            \"Complete transport and combined passive-plus-transport cost, memory and timestep restrictions are measured at approved resolutions; findings do not claim active adoption.\"\n          ],\n          \"plan_review\": null,\n          \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-field\", \"AR-geometry\", \"AR-passive-coupling\", \"AR-passive-qualification\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Give shared consumers one distinct species implementation artifact without duplicating the design contract.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"add_artifact\",\n        \"artifact\": {\n          \"id\": \"AR-species\",\n          \"title\": \"Conservative species transport implementation\",\n          \"description\": \"Declared species advection/diffusion using shared flow fluxes and side-separated moving geometry, staged amount ownership and boundary accounts, with stationary and moving/passive reference, positivity, rollback and cost checks. Excludes finite ports, permeability and reactions.\",\n          \"produced_by\": \"T-species\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Block resource implementation on passive review and consume the extracted species implementation explicitly; actuation inherits this gate through T-transfers.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-transfers\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Proceed only after favorable T-passive-qualification review and completion of T-species. Implement the transfer/reaction portion of AR-work-package against field, species, chamber and geometry interfaces. Use AR-passive-qualification's supported limits; its existence alone is not approval. Exercise static or prescribed geometry first, then verify paired transfers through the established moving/passive schedule using AR-species. Exclude rupture, growth, repair and heat.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"depends_on\",\n            \"value\": [\"T-core\", \"T-chambers\", \"T-field\", \"T-geometry\", \"T-schedule-design\", \"T-passive-qualification\", \"T-species\"]\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"input_artifacts\",\n            \"value\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-chambers\", \"AR-field\", \"AR-geometry\", \"AR-work-package\", \"AR-passive-qualification\", \"AR-species\"]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Explicitly compose the separated species package into the active prototype while preserving existing inputs and later adoption.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-prototype\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Compose AR-passive-coupling, AR-species, AR-transfers, and AR-actuators using the approved fixture after the favorable passive qualification gate. Use bitloop and traces capabilities via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md and its references/tracing-diagnostics.md. Keep Substrate/Substrate.h and .cpp thin; place construction and telemetry outside core ownership. Passive qualification and focused transport checks do not replace T-adoption's later active coupled campaign.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"depends_on\",\n            \"value\": [\"T-passive-coupling\", \"T-transfers\", \"T-actuators\", \"T-schedule-design\", \"T-species\"]\n          },\n  