                            "output": {
                                "identity": "fnv1a64:d93c4bf29f1af770",
                                "lines": "1: # F-pilot: reproducible Bitloop diagnostic pilot\n2: \n3: Task: `T-pilot`. Capabilities used: `bitloop`, `traces`, `snapshots-checkpoints`.\n4: This is a C-app lifecycle/wiring fixture, not a simulation or solver prototype.\n5: \n6: ## Fixture and oracle\n7: \n8: `Substrate/Substrate.h` and `.cpp` keep development-only counters under\n9: `BITLOOP_DEV_MODE`. `sceneStart()` resets them; `sceneProcess()` increments the\n10: tick count and accumulates `frame_dt() * 0.001` seconds. The active framework's\n11: `ProjectBase::processHeadlessFrame(dt)` supplies `frame_dt` in milliseconds.\n12: Drawing and tracing only read the counters. Explicit scene IDs are\n13: `substrate-0`, `substrate-1`, etc.; the default layout contains one scene.\n14: \n15: Use eight updates at `dt = 0.125 s`. Post-process frame `f` must report\n16: `ticks = f + 1` and `time = (f + 1) / 8 s`, matching the runner's time.\n17: The threshold is exact equality (zero seconds error), justified by the short,\n18: binary-exact fixture; it is **not** a physical tolerance. No RNG is used and no\n19: seed, input replay, or scene configuration override is required.\n20: \n21: The one-second horizon checks startup, repeated processing, unit conversion,\n22: trace output and a final draw. It supplies no behavioral/endurance coverage for\n23: physics. The retained fixture supports replay of this wiring check; remove or\n24: replace its counters when real project telemetry supersedes it.\n25: \n26: ## Tested build context\n27: \n28: - Project HEAD before pilot edits: `96c371f76ea9aac8a1306f49ab4aea81ea09668f`.\n29:   Pre-existing dirty/untracked user files were preserved.\n30: - Root CMake target: `Substrate`; executable: `build/msvc-release-codex/app/app.exe`.\n31: - Ninja, Release, Windows x64, MSVC `19.51.36257.0`, `BITLOOP_DEV_MODE=ON`.\n32: - Provider: local `../../bitloop`, manifest version `0.9.20`, HEAD\n33:   `23ea316e8325519bca89c14c43bbe0df134455f4` **with existing modifications**.\n34:   A commit alone does not reproduce that framework; retained hashes identify\n35:   the actual source inputs.\n36: - Existing third-party installation:\n37:   `build/ninja-debug/vcpkg_installed/x64-windows`, used read-only.\n38:   `VCPKG_MANIFEST_INSTALL=OFF`; no dependency or registry was changed.\n39: - Compilation and execution establish compatibility with these local sources\n40:   and installed libraries. Detached package-backed compatibility was not tested;\n41:   no claim is made about registry availability of matching diagnostic APIs.\n42: \n43: For this workspace, the ignored `CMakeUserPresets.json` contains the following\n44: configure preset and a matching build preset targeting `Substrate`. Preserve\n45: other entries when recreating it:\n46: \n47: ```json\n48: {\n49:   \"version\": 3,\n50:   \"configurePresets\": [{\n51:     \"name\": \"msvc-release-codex\",\n52:     \"inherits\": \"ninja-release\",\n53:     \"binaryDir\": \"${sourceDir}/build/msvc-release-codex\",\n54:     \"cacheVariables\": {\n55:       \"BUILD_FLAVOR\": \"msvc-release-codex\",\n56:       \"CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE\": \"${sourceDir}/../../.vcpkg/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake\",\n57:       \"VCPKG_INSTALLED_DIR\": \"${sourceDir}/build/ninja-debug/vcpkg_installed\",\n58:       \"VCPKG_MANIFEST_INSTALL\": \"OFF\",\n59:       \"BITLOOP_PROVIDER\": \"SOURCE\",\n60:       \"BITLOOP_SOURCE_DIR\": \"${sourceDir}/../../bitloop\",\n61:       \"BITLOOP_DEV_MODE\": \"ON\",\n62:       \"BITLOOP_BUILD_TESTS\": \"OFF\"\n63:     }\n64:   }],\n65:   \"buildPresets\": [{\n66:     \"name\": \"msvc-release-codex\",\n67:     \"configurePreset\": \"msvc-release-codex\",\n68:     \"targets\": [\"Substrate\"]\n69:   }]\n70: }\n71: ```\n72: \n73: The source checkout, installed dependency tree, VS C++ tools and a working SDL3/\n74: OpenGL rendering context are prerequisites. On another machine, first verify\n75: the appropriate existing provider/dependencies; do not silently substitute or\n76: upgrade them. The local override above is not a portable dependency lock.\n77: \n78: Run from the project root in PowerShell, initializing the developer environment\n79: in the same shell as CMake:\n80: \n81: ```powershell\n82: $vsPath = & 'C:/Program Files (x86)/Microsoft Visual Studio/Installer/vswhere.exe' -latest -products '*' -requires Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.Tools.x86.x64 -property installationPath\n83: Import-Module \"$vsPath/Common7/Tools/Microsoft.VisualStudio.DevShell.dll\"\n84: Enter-VsDevShell -VsInstallPath $vsPath -SkipAutomaticLocation -DevCmdArguments '-arch=x64 -host_arch=x64'\n85: cmake --preset msvc-release-codex\n86: cmake --build --preset msvc-release-codex --parallel 8\n87: ```\n88: \n89: ## Launch and check\n90: \n91: Create a new sequential `.codex/runs/runNNNN_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` folder, preserving\n92: earlier runs. Assign its absolute path to `$run` below. The recorded run used\n93: `run0003_20261009_130412`. Use `Start-Process -Wait -PassThru`: direct invocation\n94: of this Windows GUI-subsystem executable can return without setting\n95: `$LASTEXITCODE`.\n96: \n97: ```powershell\n98: $exe = (Resolve-Path build/msvc-release-codex/app/app.exe).Path\n99: $p = Start-Process $exe -ArgumentList '--headless --project Substrate --list-scenes' -WindowStyle Hidden -Wait -PassThru -RedirectStandardOutput \"$run/scenes.json\" -RedirectStandardError \"$run/scenes.stderr.log\"\n100: if ($p.ExitCode -ne 0) { throw \"Scene listing failed: $($p.ExitCode)\" }\n101: $common = '--headless --project Substrate --scene substrate-0 --frames 8 --dt 0.125 --surface 800x600 --trace-format full'\n102: $p = Start-Process $exe -ArgumentList \"$common --trace `\"$run/primary`\" --snapshots --snapshot-every-frames 8\" -WindowStyle Hidden -Wait -PassThru -RedirectStandardOutput \"$run/primary.log\" -RedirectStandardError \"$run/primary.stderr.log\"\n103: if ($p.ExitCode -ne 0) { throw \"Primary run failed: $($p.ExitCode)\" }\n104: $p = Start-Process $exe -ArgumentList \"$common --trace `\"$run/replay`\"\" -WindowStyle Hidden -Wait -PassThru -RedirectStandardOutput \"$run/replay.log\" -RedirectStandardError \"$run/replay.stderr.log\"\n105: if ($p.ExitCode -ne 0) { throw \"Replay failed: $($p.ExitCode)\" }\n106: ./tooling/check_pilot.ps1 -Run $run\n107: ```\n108: \n109: The checker validates all 16 observations, configuration, completion, exact\n110: times/ticks, empty physical objects/events, byte-identical replay traces, a\n111: selectable scene, and snapshot metadata/file existence. Separately inspect the\n112: image; the script does not judge pixels. Full traces need no delta reconstruction.\n113: \n114: ## Recorded result and artifact map\n115: \n116: All paths below are relative to\n117: `.codex/runs/run0003_20261009_130412/` unless stated otherwise.\n118: \n119: | F-pilot part | Concrete reference and guarantee |\n120: | --- | --- |\n121: | Instructions and fixture | This document; `Substrate/Substrate.h`, `Substrate/Substrate.cpp`; project-owned lifecycle counters, no physics |\n122: | Executable build | `configure.log`, `build-final.log`, `CMakeUserPresets.json`, `CMakeCache.txt`; actual successful local target/configuration |\n123: | Input identity | `source-hashes.json`, `dependency-status.txt`, `project-status-before.txt`, `pilot-source.patch`; source and installed dependency identities, including dirty source context |\n124: | Launch selection | `scenes.json`; `substrate-0` is default and selectable |\n125: | Observations | `primary/frames.jsonl`, `replay/frames.jsonl`, corresponding `metadata.json` and `summary.json`; 8 processed/traced frames per run |\n126: | Automated oracle | Project `tooling/check_pilot.ps1`, retained `checks.json`; 16 exact observations, zero maximum time error |\n127: | Inspected image | `primary/snapshots/frame_00000007_0_periodic_frame.webp`, `primary/snapshots.jsonl`; 800x600, frame 7, time 1 s |\n128: | Compact conclusion | `observations.json`; commands, visual observation, limitations and claim scope |\n129: \n130: Both processes exited 0. Final ticks = **8**, accumulated time = **1.000 s**;\n131: all intermediate values matched exactly. Trace SHA-256 for both runs:\n132: `35C8CE2D9262F920C64A5F3ACB3F8138500FF6E762503F36C5A82AB61E7A4151`.\n133: The primary run rendered one snapshot with zero failures; the replay disabled\n134: snapshot rendering and still produced identical semantic observations.\n135: \n136: The image was actually inspected: the upper-left text reads “Diagnostic pilot -\n137: no physics”, “ticks = 8”, and “time (s) = 1.000000”, clearly visible over the\n138: existing coordinate grid. It agrees with frame 7 telemetry.\n139: \n140: The initial compile failed because pilot text coordinates used integers with\n141: the framework's floating-point transform template. The project calls were\n142: corrected to doubles; `build-initial-failure.log` retains that resolved failure.\n143: An initial launch wrapper also stopped because direct invocation yielded no\n144: exit code; explicit process waiting corrected it before the two recorded runs.\n145: No framework repair or compatibility shim was added.\n146: \n147: **INCONCLUSIVE physical claim:** passive coupled stability, conservation, fluid\n148: transport and biological activity cannot be assessed. There are zero physical\n149: objects and no solver, physical oracle, units contract or approved error budget\n150: in this fixture. Workflow success must not release physical adoption gates.\n151: Checkpoint hooks still return false; restart, scripted interactions, production\n152: mode, cross-hardware determinism and performance/endurance qualification are\n153: outside this pilot's checks. MindGraph saving, review and reload must be verified\n154: by the coordinator; this worker's report is not evidence that those occurred.\n",
                                "next_offset": null,
