            "question": "Worker's concrete plan concern: The selected no-slip stencil predicts 12.5% flow/work error and 6.25% pointwise velocity error in F-contract's 0.25 m passage at h=1/16 m. These exceed the proposed stationary gates of 2% and 0.5%. Adoption at that resolution requires review; no grid or budget change was applied.",
            "raw_response": "{\n  \"base_revision\": 4,\n  \"outcome\": \"keep_plan\",\n  \"reason\": \"The inspected flow specification documents a genuine rejection of the four-cell no-slip channel configuration, not a failure to complete T-design-flow's design assignment. Its 12.5% flow/work and 6.25% velocity errors exceed the proposed gates; successful algebra checks do not override that finding. The existing T-reconcile task must resolve this incompatibility before T-approve authorizes implementation. Neither finer resolution nor relaxed budgets are approved here. The contract's inviscid, free-slip passive fixtures are not themselves disproved by this viscous no-slip reference. Existing reconciliation, human approval and qualification gates remain appropriate.\",\n  \"evidence_ids\": [\n    \"evidence-4e1e250b-73d6-425e-a945-8f54f3228348\"\n  ],\n  \"changes\": [],\n  \"task_actions\": [],\n  \"follow_up\": null,\n  \"recovery\": null,\n  \"accepted_results\": []\n}",
