                                "identity": "fnv1a64:db192b4e45aa7000",
                                "lines": "481: all retries. Separate startup, steady and narrow-passage windows; never amortize\n482: a failed solve out of the sample. Report mean/p95/p99/max and actual simulated\n483: seconds divided by wall seconds, with actual CPU/compiler/precision/worker state.\n484: Keep F-contract's proposed complete-work limits as future gates; no performance\n485: claim follows from sparsity or an estimated iteration count. IC triangular solves\n486: and long thin components may limit parallel throughput; measure rather than\n487: assume that 16 workers accelerate them.\n488: \n489: ## 9. Qualification and downstream handoff\n490: \n491: Before running acceptance, approve fixture coefficients, thresholds and hardware;\n492: implement independently checked operators/oracles; then use the existing Bitloop\n493: trace workflow through C-app. Every trial/commit checks finite state, inventories,\n494: connectivity, component compatibility, residuals and energy. Reference cases have\n495: every-step local checks; retain compact extrema/first failure, selected field maps\n496: and fixed-time summaries rather than dumping all fields every frame.\n497: \n498: For refinement use F-contract's factor-0.7 improvement rule and its 0.01-times-\n499: acceptance-limit floor, with frozen physical geometry. Preserve the 0.25 m gap\n500: as h changes. R0 assesses exact discrete invariants; R1 and R2 distinguish the\n501: implemented discrete law from continuum error; R3 exposes narrow-boundary risk.\n502: None implements F-contract Q1–Q6 moving geometry or content/mechanics coupling.\n503: Later boundary design must provide sided cuts and conservative operators compatible\n504: with this layout, and physical pressure references for sealed deformable interiors.\n505: That compatibility must be demonstrated rather than inferred from the matrix form.\n506: \n507: Restart will require owned inventories/momenta, actual time/revision, domain/port\n508: identities, material/boundary configuration and any pressure warm-start or cache\n509: state that changes continuation. Rebuildable stencils/factors can be omitted only\n510: with a declared deterministic reconstruction. No checkpoint implementation is\n511: added here; F-contract remains authoritative on rollback and continuation tests.\n512: \n513: ## 10. Task verification record\n514: \n515: The task inspects the actual F-contract, project instructions, current source and\n516: selected-task metadata. No required input is inferred solely from an artifact ID.\n517: The specification maps acceptance as follows: sections 2–6 define storage, flux,\n518: boundaries/nullspaces and advancement; section 7 supplies worked references/local\n519: and work oracles; sections 5, 6 and 8 cover disconnected/narrow regions and\n520: pressure-iteration/memory instrumentation.\n521: \n522: Numerical tables are direct binary64 PowerShell evaluations of the printed\n523: formulas, not a solver execution. Further algebra checks verify the channel\n524: stencil at every row, its wall-force/work balance, the shear-mode BE energy split,\n525: and a two-cell pressure projection's sign, divergence and energy loss.\n526: \n527: PowerShell binary64 audit, executed during T-design-flow:\n528: \n529: | Calculation checked | Actual observation | Arithmetic audit threshold |\n530: | --- | --- | --- |\n531: | R1, Ny=16, every discrete steady row: `mu L_h u+G` | Maximum residual 7.08e-16 N/m² | ≤1e-12 N/m² |\n532: | R1 stress quadratic versus driving power | Both 0.016796875 W; difference 0 W | ≤1e-12 W |\n533: | R2 first BE step, a_old=0.1 m/s, Ny=16, Delta t=0.00125 s | Physical loss 4.82458743374e-5 J; numerical loss 1.17519952287e-7 J; identity error 1.17e-18 J | ≤1e-14 J |\n534: | Two unit-area cells, one unit-length free face, m_f=1 kg, u*=1 m/s, Delta t=0.00125 s; pin p_a=0, p_b=800 N/m | Final u=0 and divergence=0; projection loss 0.5 J; energy identity residual 0 J | ≤1e-14 for velocity/energy checks in their respective units |\n535: | R3 minimum-gap channel formula | Q=0.00130208333333 versus Q_h=0.00146484375 m²/s; 12.5% error | Exceeds proposed 2% flow/work gate; known candidate limitation |\n536: \n537: The two-cell check is an operator sign/energy calculation with a deliberately\n538: non-solenoidal predictor, not an admissible initialized flow run. These arithmetic\n539: tolerances check the written formulas; they do not replace physical qualification\n540: budgets or demonstrate convergence/iteration counts of an implemented solver.\n541: Tables at Ny=16/32/64 were recalculated; local error and integrated flow/work\n542: error were kept separate. The negative R3 result is retained for review rather\n543: than hidden by the successful algebra checks.\n544: \n545: Document checks inspect all three task acceptance groups, the fixed choice of\n546: method, local and global oracles, proposed-value labels, existing local links,\n547: and dimensional consistency. Production source and F-contract hashes are checked\n548: against their retained/input identities. No build, solver run, memory measurement\n549: or runtime performance result is claimed for this documentation-only task.\n550: Production source, F-contract, build configuration, dependencies and framework\n551: code are unchanged by this task.\n",
