            "question": "Worker's concrete plan concern: Existing numerical limits remain: the 0.25 m no-slip passage at h=1/16 m predicts 12.5% flow error versus the proposed 2% gate; Q4's reduced interior predicts speed/c=0.817 versus 0.1. The stationary incompressible law also cannot support sealed volume-changing interiors without an additional physical closure. These require review before affected qualification.",
            "raw_response": "{\n  \"base_revision\": 4,\n  \"outcome\": \"keep_plan\",\n  \"reason\": \"The inspected boundary specification preserves the known passage and Q4 failures and correctly identifies another limit: sealed incompressible interiors cannot change area or obtain physical wall pressure from an arbitrary pressure gauge. These are design compatibility findings, not failure to complete T-design-boundary. Existing T-reconcile must resolve the interior closure and fixture compatibility before T-approve authorizes implementation. The worked geometry references and reported arithmetic checks do not establish coupled physical validity. No relaxed budgets, changed fixtures or solver adoption are approved; the existing reconciliation and approval gates remain appropriate.\",\n  \"evidence_ids\": [\n    \"evidence-1567cd7e-772a-4bc0-aa8d-a39f9d8d04a5\"\n  ],\n  \"changes\": [],\n  \"task_actions\": [],\n  \"follow_up\": null,\n  \"recovery\": null,\n  \"accepted_results\": []\n}",
