                                "lines": "381: 4. Test a tiny isolated pocket, a zero-length aperture, a wet gap below 0.25 m,\n382:    ambiguous intersection, nonpositive IC pivot and exhausted solver cap. Verify\n383:    rejection with the last committed state/time unchanged, never a disappearing\n384:    wall, erased amount or frozen motion. These are negative controls.\n385: \n386: Use all F-contract section 6 budgets without relaxation: local area error\n387: <=1e-7 h² and each nonzero fragment relative error <=1e-5, global area error\n388: <=1e-8 A*, accumulated absolute sweep mismatch <=1e-6 A*; actual forbidden\n389: transfer exactly absent; facet normal-flux error <=1e-8 U* times length.\n390: Local volume defect is <=1e-8 actual fragment area per substep and divergence\n391: defect <=1e-6 s^-1. Mass/impulse, local and cumulative energy, deformation and\n392: force/torque/work budgets also apply. Agglomeration never changes their denominators.\n393: \n394: ## 6. Worked geometry and account references\n395: \n396: These are binary64 arithmetic oracles, not executions of a flow solver. Use\n397: h=1/16 m, delta=0.00125 s and rho=1 kg/m² unless stated. Local cells below are\n398: geometry primitives; their width is not a physical passage below g_min.\n399: \n400: ### B1. Moving corner: keep the cross term\n401: \n402: In one h by h cell a solid occupies [0,a] by [0,b]. Initially a=b=0.5h;\n403: then a1=0.51h, b1=0.505h. The remaining L-shaped fluid is one connected fragment.\n404: The solid area increases by 0.00755h²=2.94921875e-5 m². Fluid area decreases\n405: from 0.75h² to 0.74245h². Integrating the moving vertical and horizontal faces:\n406: \n407: ```text\n408: S_fluid = -[(b0+b1)/2 Delta a + (a0+a1)/2 Delta b]\n409:         = -2.94921875e-5 m².\n410: ```\n411: \n412: Uniform u=(0.5,0.25) m/s has the required free-slip wall normal motion. Integrate\n413: its flux through the actual outer apertures: top/right outflow less left/bottom\n414: inflow is +2.94921875e-5 m². Thus Delta M=-2.94921875e-5 kg,\n415: Delta P=u Delta M, and Delta K=0.5|u|² Delta M=-4.608154296875e-6 J, all carried\n416: by open-face advection. At uniform p=2 N/m, wall work pS=-5.8984375e-5 J; the\n417: work delivered to the reservoir is its opposite. In the fluid ledger, wall work\n418: input and reservoir pressure work output cancel. They do not replace advected energy.\n419: \n420: Using old facet lengths gives 0.0075h² and misses Delta a Delta b=\n421: 1.953125e-7 m², far above the proposed 1e-7h² local geometric budget. This\n422: deliberately wrong sweep is a negative control, even though endpoint drawings\n423: would show the correct final corner.\n424: \n425: ### B2. Thin membrane: support birth and death on separate sides\n426: \n427: Take adjacent cells [0,h] and [h,2h], each of height h, with a vertical membrane\n428: extending past the patch. Move it from x0=0.995h to x1=1.005h at 0.5 m/s.\n429: Tag left-side fluid with Y=1 and right-side fluid with Y=0. Supply matching\n430: uniform velocity at the left/right reservoirs. There is no membrane opening.\n431: \n432: | Fragment | A0/h² | A1/h² | Net open F/h² | Delta M/rho/h² |\n433: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n434: | left in cell 0 | 0.995 | 1 | -0.005 | +0.005 |\n435: | left in cell 1, born | 0 | 0.005 | -0.005 | +0.005 |\n436: | right in cell 0, disappears | 0.005 | 0 | +0.005 | -0.005 |\n437: | right in cell 1 | 1 | 0.995 | +0.005 | -0.005 |\n438: \n439: The grid face x=h carries right-side flux during the first half-interval and\n440: left-side flux during the second: each is 0.005h²=1.953125e-5 m². They are\n441: different sided records. Outer inflow and outflow are each 0.01h²=\n442: 3.90625e-5 m². Every row satisfies F+Delta A=0; total mass is unchanged, left\n443: mass increases only from its reservoir and right mass decreases only to its\n444: reservoir. Newly uncovered fragments do not receive the opposite-side tracer.\n445: Merge the 0.005-fraction support only with its same-side neighbour.\n446: \n447: For p_left=2 and p_right=0.5 N/m, force on this membrane segment is 0.09375 N\n448: to the right, impulse 0.0001171875 kg m/s and work 5.859375e-5 J. Left/right\n449: wall pressure work is respectively +7.8125e-5 and -1.953125e-5 J. Support and\n450: reservoir ledgers close the prescribed-motion case; an unforced wall must instead\n451: respond dynamically. A shared Cartesian cell index cannot justify pooling its\n452: two fluids. The checker demonstrates that such pooling contaminates the tagged\n453: sides even while conserving total mass.\n454: \n455: ### B3. Narrow supported passage: conservation is not accuracy\n456: \n457: Retain the supplemental stationary no-slip channel from F-flow-law: length 2 m,\n458: gap H=0.25 m, mu=0.1 kg/s, pressure-gradient equivalent G=0.1 N/m², periodic\n459: axial flow with a metered body force. The selected stencil gives\n460: \n461: ```text\n462: Q = G H³/(12 mu) = 0.00130208333333333 m²/s\n463: Q_h = Q + G H h²/(6 mu) = 0.00146484375 m²/s\n464: power_h = G length Q_h = 0.00029296875 W.\n465: ```\n466: \n467: Mass through two cross-sections is equal and opposite. Discrete drive power and\n468: the stencil's viscous dissipation agree, yet Q_h is 12.5% too large. At 8 and\n469: 16 cells across the same physical gap the errors are 3.125% and 0.78125%; the\n470: corresponding peak-normalized velocity errors are 1.5625% and 0.390625%.\n471: The base case therefore fails the proposed quality gates without any leakage.\n472: \n473: Translate both walls together by the offsets in section 5, preserving H. Cut\n474: slivers join only fluid inside the passage; never join through either wall.\n475: Compare flux, pressure drop and work to the same reference, including grouping\n476: transitions. Then narrow below 0.25 m: the supported outcome is a bounded failure,\n477: not a silently sealed passage or a pressure connection through solid. This task\n478: does not authorize adopting finer resolution or changing the gates.\n479: \n480: ### B4. Freely expanding chamber: actual polygon and paired work\n481: \n482: Use the actual Q1 N=128 polygon, R0=1 m, A0=(N/2)sin(2pi/N)=\n483: 3.140331156954753 m², M=1.1A0 kg, rho0=1, B_bulk=10 N/m. For a short geometric\n484: slice R=1 to R1=1.000125 m, actual Delta A=A0(R1²-1), about\n485: 7.851318569e-4 m². All 128 facets have the same integrated sweep Delta A/128.\n486: The contents mass remains M. The exterior's total cut area decreases by Delta A\n487: and its reservoir carries rho_f Delta A outwards. No mass crosses the membrane.\n488: An initial exterior tracer remains exterior.\n489: \n490: Use U(A,M) from F-contents-law. Its secant pressure gives p_sec Delta A=-Delta U\n491: exactly to arithmetic tolerance. Differentiating the polygon shoelace area at\n492: the midpoint vertices gives the same work and paired vertex forces. Using pi R²\n493: in the pressure law while clipping the polygon produces a relative area mismatch\n494: of about 4.0174e-4; it is not harmless quadrature at the contract's area budget.\n495: \n496: This finite slice verifies geometry and mean compression work only. It is not\n497: a constant-speed physical expansion solution. For the independent circular\n498: continuum Q1 reference, at R=1.02 m and Rdot=0.1 m/s, use its acceleration equation\n499: to obtain Rddot=0.308980074751185 m/s². Include K_contents=M Rdot²/4,\n500: K_exterior=pi rho (R Rdot)² ln(4/R), membrane energy pi S(R-1)² and compression\n501: energy. Their total derivative plus outer kinetic-energy flux\n502: `pi rho (R Rdot)³/4²` is zero. This separately checks the inertial and exterior\n503: work terms required by the inputs. Polygon-vs-circle error must converge with N;\n504: it must not be hidden by replacing the actual chamber area.\n505: \n506: ## 7. Qualification and complete-work boundaries\n507: \n508: This document's executed checks are specification/arithmetic checks only. Future\n509: qualification uses the contract's 2 s Q0–Q5 rejection screen plus Q6 failures,\n510: then 20/40 s and, if required, 80 s behavioral windows and at least 20 measured\n511: Q1 periods. Include grid phases, rotations, small-fraction events and every B1–B4\n512: primitive above. Q4/reduced-interior and the base no-slip passage remain pending\n513: review of their known incompatible limits; a correct negative result is not adoption.\n514: \n515: Run temporal dt/2 and dt/4 comparisons and spatial (h/2,2N,dt/2),\n516: (h/4,4N,dt/4), preserving all physical gaps and coefficients. Inherit the 0.7\n517: successive-difference criterion above the contract's 0.01-budget refinement floor.\n518: Inspect local fields and grouping-transition peaks as well as global sums. The\n519: small-cell strategy has not earned acceptance until those continuity/refinement\n520: and full coupled work budgets pass; arithmetic conservation is necessary only.\n521: \n522: Complete calculated-interval cost includes collision/swept-event detection,\n523: clipping and independent geometry checks, primal/dual agglomeration, overlap\n524: remaps, reconstruction and flux lifting, both pressure projections and IC rebuilds,\n525: viscosity, mechanics and content inertia, outer passes, safety scans, failed\n526: attempts and commit. Report each count and sum, maximum group diameter/size,\n527: minimum raw cut fraction and physical gap, component/gauge counts, true local\n528: residual maxima, and accepted/requested time. Memory includes committed and staged\n529: owner state, event histories, maps, factors, overlap tables and peak scratch.\n530: No scratch or rejected work is excluded. Rendering/recording/checkpoint costs\n531: remain separately reported. Inherit the proposed single-chamber mean 20 ms/H,\n532: p95 40 ms, max 100 ms and 256 MiB screen; do not extrapolate laboratory throughput.\n533: \n534: Raw implemented diagnostic runs will use the next project `.codex/runs/runNNNN_...`\n535: folder. This task executes no simulation, so its durable evidence is the focused\n536: checker and the compact observations below, not a fabricated run directory.\n537: \n538: ## 8. Sources and interpretation\n539: \n540: The candidate and its equations above are project design choices. Literature\n541: supports the need to check geometric conservation and pressure transients, not\n542: the claim that this particular coupling works: [Seo and Mittal, 2011](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3156558/)\n543: analyse moving-boundary geometric conservation and virtual merging; their method\n544: does not establish this design's momentum/work closure. [An accurate moving boundary formulation in cut-cell methods](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0021999112005839)\n545: report that conservative cell merging alone need not eliminate pressure\n546: oscillations. Thus continuity and local work tests remain explicit adoption gates.\n547: \n548: ## 9. Executed specification checks and reproducibility\n549: \n550: Used capability guidance: **bitloop**, **simulation-health**; read the local\n551: bitloop-development entry and simulation-health reference. No Bitloop API changes,\n552: package installation, physical runtime, visual claim or checkpoint claim is made.\n553: \n554: Run from the Substrate root:\n555: \n556: ```powershell\n557: ./tooling/check_boundary_law.ps1 -Document\n558: git diff --check\n559: ```\n560: \n561: The checker validates B1 corner flux/mass/momentum/pressure work, B2 sided\n562: birth/death and membrane work, positive same-side remap conservation and kinetic\n563: loss, the pressure projection work identity, B3 channel arithmetic, B4 polygon\n564: sweeps/area-gradient work and the continuous radial energy identity. It includes\n565: negative controls for frozen corner sweeps, opposite-side pooling, an isolated\n566: small region and incompatible closed-volume change. Its tolerances check algebra\n567: in binary64, not the unapproved physical qualification budgets.\n568: \n569: Input SHA-256 identities (also checked by `-Document`):\n570: \n571: | Input | SHA-256 |\n572: | --- | --- |\n573: | PHYSICAL_CONTRACT.md | 48FF446850E0DD31A0AE5E20F803923DB9F6E22A384A9532E7144E04F4CFDC07 |\n574: | MECHANICS_LAW.md | EE2C5000A81D357CDE5F706D98F43A45C52429E543EE80333DF7964A6DF8145A |\n575: | COMPARTMENT_LAW.md | C05278878AE4A3DA7FFB1035662F2A4002BF0C8D098BC19CF80E41014AAF96B3 |\n576: | STATIONARY_FLOW_LAW.md | BC2BE2E0568DFAECBE167FD5AF4C79E57A3B3957E07E65DA1BD55CB56F5DE53A |\n577: \n578: The current pilot source hashes remain FC24DB1F60D89A1955C5DFC24EB95A15DBA86A736C03134A17B43FEA34E4F6E5\n579: (header) and F6CF93EB3AD740399016BD2AA4B4C0FB84E9C576F38338308CF69C6AA87A7FB6\n580: (source). Existing user changes and all four input specifications are preserved.\n",
