                                                "value": "Use A-scope/A-hardware/A-screen and D-contract. Define the smallest two-chamber contractile organism that swims and pumps through finite ports, with nutrient exchange and fuel use; it need not represent a named substance. Specify consistent 2D units, shapes, coefficients, minimum features, fixed resolution family, initial conditions, species and energy meanings, and environmental outer conditions. Define prototype and later 16-organism screen separately; do not adopt the 256-organism workload. Numerical tolerances are proposals for human approval, not facts supplied by the vision. Within the prototype protocol, predeclare a bounded two-way passive campaign before species/resource/activity implementation: relevant passive references, repeated externally loaded and unforced cycles, refinement comparisons, local and cumulative errors, rollback injections, full coupled cost, timescale-derived horizons, compute limits, extension rules, and rejection/inconclusive outcomes. Distinguish this campaign from focused coupling tests and later active adoption. Scope any early tracer probe as a geometric/flux reference, not full species-solver qualification."
