                                "identity": "fnv1a64:2830230c2d7df1ab",
                                "lines": "1: # F-passive-spec: reconciliation audit — blocked draft\n2: \n3: Draft 0, 2026-10-10. MindGraph task **T-reconcile**.\n4: \n5: **Incomplete: this is a retained prerequisite audit, not a frozen or implementable\n6: passive work package.** All five required specifications exist. Their numerical\n7: proposals are not mutually compatible with the proposed positive fixture suite.\n8: No reviewed resolution of those conflicts accompanies this task. The task says\n9: to stop when a required decision is missing; dependent reconciliation and the\n10: configuration freeze stop here. This is not a request for routine numerical\n11: approval merely because values are labelled unapproved: there are specific\n12: contradictions below which require selecting different fixtures, validity policy\n13: or a physical interior law.\n14: \n15: No input law, threshold, source, dependency or build configuration was changed.\n16: No task outside T-reconcile was started. The working tree already contains the\n17: earlier diagnostic pilot and design documents; those changes are preserved.\n18: \n19: ## 1. Verified inputs and project boundary\n20: \n21: | Artifact | Actual input | SHA-256 |\n22: | --- | --- | --- |\n23: | F-contract | [PHYSICAL_CONTRACT.md](PHYSICAL_CONTRACT.md), draft 1.1 | 48FF446850E0DD31A0AE5E20F803923DB9F6E22A384A9532E7144E04F4CFDC07 |\n24: | F-mechanics-law | [MECHANICS_LAW.md](MECHANICS_LAW.md), draft 1 | EE2C5000A81D357CDE5F706D98F43A45C52429E543EE80333DF7964A6DF8145A |\n25: | F-contents-law | [COMPARTMENT_LAW.md](COMPARTMENT_LAW.md), draft 1 | C05278878AE4A3DA7FFB1035662F2A4002BF0C8D098BC19CF80E41014AAF96B3 |\n26: | F-flow-law | [STATIONARY_FLOW_LAW.md](STATIONARY_FLOW_LAW.md), draft 1 | BC2BE2E0568DFAECBE167FD5AF4C79E57A3B3957E07E65DA1BD55CB56F5DE53A |\n27: | F-boundary-law | [BOUNDARY_LAW.md](BOUNDARY_LAW.md), draft 1 | 55AF302183C77850586133D704BD0A6139B72CFD966C7853D13229A507E13EFF |\n28: \n29: Inspected [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md), the local bitloop-development skill and its\n30: advanced-project-workflow/simulation-health guidance. Used capability IDs\n31: **bitloop** and **simulation-health**. This is a single audit stage; the plan is\n32: to verify prerequisites, test compatibility, and proceed to reconciliation only\n33: if that gate passes. No delegation, runtime changes or trajectory experiment.\n34: \n35: [CMakeLists.txt](../CMakeLists.txt) declares `bitloop_new_project(Substrate ...)`.\n36: The [header](../Substrate/Substrate.h) and [scene](../Substrate/Substrate.cpp)\n37: still contain only pilot tick/time observations, with checkpoint hooks returning\n38: false. No physical kernel or coupled build compatibility is inferred from that\n39: pilot. A build or headless run would not resolve the analytic conflicts here.\n40: \n41: ## 2. Compatibility observations\n42: \n43: All following measurements are binary64 evaluations of the specified reference\n44: equations, not observed runtime trajectories. Source thresholds are the current,\n45: **PROPOSED / UNAPPROVED** input revisions; this audit does not replace them.\n46: No random seed is used, and no simulated horizon is executed.\n47: \n48: ### 2.1 Q3 translation violates the contents screen at startup\n49: \n50: F-contract section 5.2 prescribes the regular N=128, R=1 m polygon with\n51: `c_x(t)=0.5 sin²(pi t/2)` m and a 2 s period. Differentiating gives\n52: `c_x''(0)=pi²/4=2.4674011002723395 m/s²`.\n53: \n54: For the contents law's pure translation, `v=c_dot` and\n55: `pi_inertial(x)=-rho a_c dot (x-c)` (sections 3.2 and 6.1). The actual base\n56: polygon contains vertices at x-c_x=+1 and -1 m. Its density is 1 kg/m² and\n57: `c_sound²=B/rho0=10 m²/s²`. Therefore, exactly for this polygon:\n58: \n59: ```text\n60: max |pi_inertial| = 2.4674011002723395 N/m\n61: max |pi_inertial|/(rho c_sound²) = 0.24674011002723395\n62: required by F-contents-law section 5: <= 0.01\n63: ```\n64: \n65: The proposed pressure-variation screen fails by a factor of 24.674. The acoustic\n66: crossing-time ratio is `(2 m/c_sound)/(2 s)=0.31622776601683794`, also above its\n67: 0.1 screen. Relative translation velocity is zero, so testing only the relative\n68: Mach number would miss the failure. The prescribed motion starts at zero velocity,\n69: but has nonzero acceleration; zero instantaneous power is not a validity proof.\n70: The integrated polygon pressure force is still `-M a_c`, so correct global\n71: impulse accounting does not cure the local model-validity violation.\n72: \n73: Halving dt cannot reduce an acceleration fixed by the physical fixture. Under\n74: the present validity policy this is an invalid configuration/startup response,\n75: not a pressure-solver problem that bounded retries can repair. The positive Q3\n76: qualification cannot be frozen with both these inputs unchanged.\n77: \n78: ### 2.2 Q2 compression also exceeds the same screen at startup\n79: \n80: The prescribed scale is `R(t)=1-0.05[1-cos(pi t)]`, so at t=0,\n81: R=1 m, Rdot=0 and Rddot=-0.05pi² m/s². For uniform affine dilation the zero-mean\n82: inertial pressure is\n83: `pi_inertial=-rho Rddot/(2R) [|r|²-<|r|²>]`.\n84: The actual polygon has `<|r|²>=(2+cos(2pi/128))/6` m². Its maximum pressure\n85: magnitude occurs at the outer vertices, giving\n86: \n87: ```text\n88: max |pi_inertial|/(rho c_sound²)\n89:   = (0.05pi²)[1-(2+cos(2pi/128))/6]/20\n90:   = 0.0123419589891695 > 0.01.\n91: ```\n92: \n93: The acoustic crossing-time ratio is again 0.3162277660 > 0.1. This is an\n94: actual-polygon reference, not substitution of a circle for authoritative area.\n95: It expands the known conflict beyond Q4. No inference is made here that all\n96: other fixtures pass the contents validity checks; that audit must continue after\n97: the model/configuration decision.\n98: \n99: ### 2.3 Previously reported Q4 and passage conflicts remain\n100: \n101: Recalculation of F-contents-law section 6.2 gives the Q4 continuum ellipse\n102: reference `u_peak=2.5836294154384025 m/s`, hence\n103: `u_peak/c_sound=0.8170153582594749 > 0.1`. This preserves the continuum-reference\n104: qualification limitation stated in that input; it is not a new polygon run.\n105: \n106: F-flow-law section 7 R3 gives, for its supplemental no-slip channel with physical\n107: gap 0.25 m and h=1/16 m, four cells across the gap. The selected stencil's errors\n108: are `2/Ny²=12.5%` for flow/work and `1/Ny²=6.25%` for peak-normalized pointwise\n109: velocity, against proposed 2% and 0.5% gates. This does not establish those errors\n110: for the inviscid free-slip Q5 fixture. Sixteen cells across the same gap predicts\n111: 0.78125% and 0.390625%, respectively, but the flow input explicitly says that this\n112: is not authorization to refine the whole coupled experiment or weaken its budget.\n113: No grid selection or cost claim for that higher-quality configuration is made here.\n114: \n115: F-boundary-law section 1 and F-flow-law section 5.3 also state that the stationary\n116: incompressible law lacks an absolute-pressure/compressibility closure for a\n117: sealed volume-changing resolved interior. Its compatibility equation cannot accept\n118: nonzero total swept area in a sealed constant-density region. Selecting that law\n119: as an automatic replacement for the invalid contents reduction would leave a\n120: physical closure missing; a pinned pressure gauge cannot provide it.\n121: \n122: ## 3. Required decision before continuing\n123: \n124: The missing decision is how to resolve the incompatible positive qualification\n125: fixtures and model validity, not whether to acknowledge their existence. Supply\n126: an explicitly reviewed amendment identifying the authoritative fixture/model\n127: revision and treatment of the known negative cases:\n128: \n129: * Resolve the prescribed Q2/Q3/Q4 motion scales against **all** contents validity\n130:   screens, or specify an authorized interior model change. Do not merely weaken\n131:   one limit until an existing case passes. A new resolved compressible interior\n132:   would be another numerical design, outside this reconciliation task.\n133: * Decide the quality-matched passage configuration and its place in the passive\n134:   gate. Preserve the four-cell result as negative evidence. A fast coarse run\n135:   cannot supply the full-cost acceptance result for a finer passing configuration.\n136: * Identify which cases remain mandatory positive tests and which are explicit\n137:   rejection controls. Relabelling Q2/Q3/Q4 as expected failures would change the\n138:   qualification scope and cannot silently count as a reconciled positive suite.\n139: \n140: The T-loop continuation approval in the earlier handoff did not approve these\n141: numerical changes. The current T-reconcile request carries no such decision.\n142: Neither source comments nor successful algebra scripts supply it. No applied\n143: MindGraph plan change or human acceptance is claimed by this document.\n144: \n145: ## 4. Existing agreements retained for resumption\n146: \n147: These are inspected input agreements, not a newly frozen execution schedule:\n148: \n149: * Use area-based units: rho in kg/m², p in N/m, and p dA in J. Species partition\n150:   mass. Structural mass, contents mass and resolved fluid mass have separate\n151:   authoritative owners; component-dual inertial masses are derived partitions.\n152:   Content inertial traction must not become a second structural mass copy.\n153: * C-world owns candidate/commit boundaries and actual time. C-boundary supplies\n154:   sided geometry and exchanges without inventory. One mechanics trajectory supplies\n155:   chamber area, grid cuts, swept area, collision and pressure-work quadrature.\n156: * The environmental disk is a p=0 reservoir with declared incoming state, not a\n157:   sealed outer wall. Opposite membrane sides do not communicate through clipping,\n158:   interpolation, preconditioners or small-cell agglomeration.\n159: * Contents-to-wall work is +p dA for expansion, plus inertial traction work;\n160:   exterior traction uses the opposite normal. Fluxes, impulses, application\n161:   points and work are posted once to both owners. Numerical residual is not fuel.\n162: * The boundary law orders a kinematic pressure predictor before transport, then\n163:   body loads, viscosity and full pressure projection. Both pressure impulses/work\n164:   enter the wall ledger. They share 200 pressure iterations per coupling pass;\n165:   discarded passes restart from committed state and do not accumulate exchanges.\n166: * Prefix commit is mandatory: accepted substeps remain; a rejected candidate\n167:   changes no committed physical state/time. The application reports actual\n168:   advancement and stops the incomplete experiment. Repeated invalid fixture\n169:   attempts cannot be treated as a successful or frozen simulation.\n170: * Finite transfer, fuel-limited stress and constrained sensing remain reserved\n171:   semantic operations, inactive in passive tests. Reservations settle only on\n172:   commit; no active algorithm or general request framework is introduced.\n173: \n174: Still unfinished: selection/verification of the coupled nonlinear convergence\n175: policy and staging layout; a compatible proposed configuration freeze with local,\n176: global and low-frequency-motion gates; quality-matched cost/horizon definitions;\n177: the full failure-injection matrix; and expected implementation/test paths. No\n178: subsystem directories or test targets were created ahead of those decisions.\n179: \n180: ## 5. Reproducible evidence and result limits\n181: \n182: From the Substrate root:\n183: \n184: ```powershell\n185: ./tooling/check_passive_reconciliation.ps1 -Document\n186: ./tooling/check_passive_reconciliation.ps1 -Document -RequireCompatible\n187: git diff --check\n188: ```\n189: \n190: The first command checks reference arithmetic, local pressure-force closure,\n191: threshold comparisons, input/source identities and this document. The second\n192: uses the same observed comparisons as a prerequisite gate and intentionally exits\n193: 2 when the current input set is incompatible. This is a failed readiness gate,\n194: not a failed evaluation of its expected negative examples. The five model/quality\n195: conditions are evaluated at startup or from analytic reference maxima; no\n196: simulation was run, so no fabricated `.codex/runs` evidence path is supplied.\n197: The durable evidence is this document and\n198: [check_passive_reconciliation.ps1](../tooling/check_passive_reconciliation.ps1).\n199: \n200: Executed on 2026-10-10 in PowerShell:\n",
                                "next_offset": 200,
