        "T-design-contents": [
            {
                "answer": "The concern is that the proposed simplified chamber model may be too simple for one of your existing tests—not that this design task failed.\n\nThink of a liquid-filled container being twisted back and forth. Pressure changes take time to travel through its contents. This model leaves out those travelling pressure waves and treats the density inside as uniform. That shortcut needs the motion to be slow enough.\n\nIn the Q4 oval-container test, the calculated internal flow reaches about 82% of the material’s sound speed. The proposed safety screen is 10%. Pressure also takes about 0.79 seconds to cross the container, compared with a 2-second motion cycle—not especially quick.\n\nSo the risk is getting plausible-looking results with unreliable wall forces and energy exchange. This is an identified mismatch between the model’s assumptions and the test, not a measured simulation failure. The thresholds themselves are still proposals.\n\nTo resolve it, the design needs either a more detailed interior model shown to handle this test, or your explicit approval to change the test’s physical scales—for example, slowing it down. Silently making the test easier would hide the problem.\n\nThe review kept the task’s work and requires this choice to be resolved before implementation approval. The calculation and limitation are in docs/COMPARTMENT_LAW.md, section 6.2.",
                "created_at": "2026-10-09 23:54 UTC",
                "error": "",
                "id": "chat-4c4d0dab8cd09054004e2accc89df5fd",
                "note": "",
                "plan_revision": 4,
                "question": "what's the concern with this? Explain it in a way I can understand.",
