        "T-reconcile": [
            {
                "answer": "Yes—this is a serious blocker to approving the current numerical package, but not evidence that the whole project is unworkable. Finding it before implementation is useful.\n\nThe reconciliation audit (F-passive-spec), in docs/PASSIVE_SPEC.md, shows that proposed positive tests conflict with the model’s own proposed validity limits. The translation test’s inertial-pressure ratio is about 25 times its limit; the compression test also fails, and both fail the acoustic-timescale screen. These are physical configuration mismatches, not errors that smaller simulation timesteps would fix.\n\nThere is a separate accuracy/cost problem: the supplemental no-slip passage predicts 12.5% flow error against a 2% target. A finer configuration is analytically promising, but its complete coupled cost has not been measured. That result should not be generalized to every passage test.\n\nThe important distinction is that this is an analytical compatibility audit, not a failed physical simulation. The reported arithmetic checks passing means the checker reproduced the contradictions—not that the proposed system passed qualification. I inspected the retained documents; I did not rerun those checks.\n\nThere is also a delivery concern. Reconcile the coupled advancement and experiment specification (T-reconcile) was meant to produce an implementable proposal. Review review-447481187569755e95fd596057560a8f recognizes the incompatibilities but explicitly rejects stopping at their discovery as sufficient completion.\n\nThe next useful deliverable is a quantified, explicitly unapproved amendment: compatible motion scales checked across complete cycles, a quality-matched passage resolution with cost implications, and the missing coupling and test policies. Preserve the failing configurations as counterexamples rather than weakening limits to hide them. If the existing laws cannot support that package, identify the precise additional model or scope decision needed.\n\nYour takeaway: keep approval blocked, but do not infer that a wholesale redesign is necessary. First establish whether the required physical behaviors can be demonstrated within the existing models’ valid range.",
                "created_at": "2026-10-10 15:05 UTC",
                "error": "",
